window.TC_PORTRAITS=Object.assign(window.TC_PORTRAITS||{},{"taurus-aries-aries":["Strike flint over a patch of clover and the field does not catch. That is something like you. People meet the Aries Rising first: a quick stride, a direct look, an opinion before the introduction ends. Your Aries Moon feels at the same speed, so a flash of temper is gone by lunch. Your Taurus Sun moves differently, deliberately and for years, and it is the part that remembers who showed up and who did not.","Moon and Rising share Aries, so what you feel and what you show are nearly one fast thing, and Mars rules both along with the whole chart. That is total coherence with little outside view, because nobody inside you is saying wait. The Taurus Sun stands one sign away from each, a semi-sextile, and sees neither clearly. Venus rules it and wants the meal to be good and the friendship to last; Mars wants a decision by noon. Much of your growing is Mars learning to enjoy what Venus builds slowly.","Momentum you can live with. You start, you say it straight, and then, unusually for a fast person, you stay for the harvest. Your reactions are honest and over by evening, your appetite is generous, and your loyalty is quiet and long. People trust that what you show is what you feel, and they are almost never wrong.","Being cornered is your real injury, and with two fire lights in front you can turn on someone who only asked a fair question. The Taurus Sun then digs in, so a flash that should have lasted a minute becomes a position held for a month out of pride. Growth is apologising while the heat is fresh, and letting the slow part of you change its mind."],"taurus-aries-taurus":["Is this worth shouting about, or should I eat first? You ask it with one hand already on the doorframe. Most people meet a calm, warm-voiced person who takes the good chair and lets conversations come to them. Then something corners you, and a short clear sentence comes out hotter than anyone expected. Ten minutes later the weather has cleared and you are offering tea. You mean both. The Aries Moon needs honesty and room to move, and the Taurus calm is the long fence it runs inside.","Sun and Rising share Taurus and speak one slow, appreciative language. The Moon in Aries sits one sign away from both, near enough to hear their footsteps and too far to read their faces. Here is the odd arithmetic: the Moon forgets a quarrel in minutes, while the fixed Sun keeps the verdict for years. So the apology you make at supper does not undo the decision you reached at noon. Mars drives your feeling and Venus governs your manner, so you want things quickly and enjoy them slowly.","Courage that does not need a crowd. You say the true thing early, then stay in the room, and your warmth makes the plainness easy to take. You recover from conflict faster than almost anyone, so people feel safe disagreeing with you, and you can start a hard job on the day it is named.","Because the Moon clears so fast, you may assume everyone else has cleared too, while the fixed Sun quietly keeps its conclusion to itself. The pattern is a flare, a warm apology, and a decision nobody was told about. Growth is saying aloud, once the flare ends, what you actually concluded, so the calm is honest as well as pleasant."],"taurus-aries-gemini":["What fifty understands and twenty cannot: the temper was never the problem. Your face is quick, funny and full of gesturing hands, so people filed the flare-ups as passing weather, and you half believed them. Looking back, you see something plainer. The Aries Moon reacts in a second, clears in a minute, and names the exact moment you were cornered. The Taurus Sun then takes its own time deciding what to do about it. Both were telling the truth.","Sun and Moon are neighbouring signs, Venus-ruled patience on one side of a wall and Mars-ruled reflex on the other, each barely able to see the other. Gemini Rising sextiles the Moon, an easy angle where air feeds fire, so a feeling gets words almost before you know it is there. That helps and it burns. You can argue brilliantly in the first minute, long before the Sun has formed the opinion it will actually keep.","Decisive warmth. You can say the true thing early and then stay for the consequences, which most fast people cannot manage. Quarrels with you tend to clear instead of fester. You begin with a spark and finish with a stubbornness that, by then, has been earned. People feel safe near someone both honest and reliable.","A flash of reaction can be followed by a month of defending the position you took inside it. The clever face lets you win arguments the Moon never wanted to have. Growth is letting the first answer cool before it hardens into the final one, and saying “give me a minute” without any shame."],"taurus-aries-cancer":["Everyone calls you calm, and your feelings still arrive faster than anyone’s. People meet the Cancer Rising first: a soft voice, a watchful kindness, an instinct for who has not eaten. The Aries Moon is what happens next. Hurt or delight lands in an instant, hot and clean, and the body wants to move: to cook, to clear the table, to say the blunt thing. Then the Taurus Sun takes its time, and by evening you know what you actually think.","The Moon rules your Cancer Rising, so the Aries Moon is the chart ruler and sets the weather for every mood. The two are square, both cardinal, fire against water: the Moon wants to act and the Rising wants to shelter, and the friction produces steam. Your Taurus Sun sits one sign from the Moon and sees it dimly, which is why the speed of your feeling can surprise you. The Sun’s help comes from the Rising, which cooperates easily, so the instinct to make a place safe is always on your side.","Warmth with momentum. You do the kind thing the same hour you think of it, forgive fast, and say what is true without a rehearsal. People relax around someone whose anger clears like weather and whose care arrives with a plate. Once you have decided to protect someone, nobody talks you out of it.","The Cancer front takes offence politely while the Moon wants to shout, so a hurt may be swallowed for a day and then leave as a clipped sentence about something small. Being cornered is the real injury, and you may arrange your whole routine so that it never happens. Growth is saying the plain Aries sentence while it is still small, before the Taurus Sun has dug in behind it."],"taurus-aries-leo":["The weight settles into your heels and the chin lifts a little, which is how a room learns you have arrived. People see warmth, generosity and an easy expectation of being liked. Inside, the Aries Moon is already half out of the door. Feeling lands fast, hot and plain, and the hands want a job to do about it. The Taurus Sun sets that urgency down at the table and asks it to sit through a meal first.","Leo Rising and the Aries Moon are both fire and trine each other, so the face you wear and the feeling you carry agree almost without effort. The Sun is another matter. It squares the Rising, the same fixed quality in a different element, and it sits one sign from the Moon without quite seeing her. So the self you are building wants slowness while the two lights around it want an audience and a starting line. You settle it by deciding fast and then defending the decision for years.","Courage with a pleasant face. You open the hard conversation warmly, take the first step of a long project and then, unlike most fire, stay for the thousandth. People follow you because the generosity is real and the pace, once you commit, is hard to stop.","Pride and speed can team up against the quieter Sun, so a slight is answered within the minute and then defended for a month. You may mistake loyalty to your first reaction for loyalty to the truth. Growth is letting one angry sentence age overnight before it turns into a position."],"taurus-aries-virgo":["A workbench in cold morning air, one chisel already out of its case and nobody else awake. That is the temperature of you. The Virgo Rising arrives tidy, observant and a little reserved, offering help before it is asked. The Aries Moon is the chisel: sudden, honest, impatient with preamble and happier with a job in its hand than a feeling in its chest. The Taurus Sun is the bench, solid enough for both.","Taurus Sun and Virgo Rising are both earth and trine, so what you are and how you arrive cooperate without noise. The Aries Moon is the outsider. It sits one sign from the Sun and a quincunx from the Rising, so neither sees it clearly, and its speed can surprise you in your own life. Mercury rules the Rising, so the mind tries to describe the feeling after the hands have already acted. The calm is real, and the fire is a guest who knows where the kitchen is.","Competence with courage. You see what needs doing and do it before the committee has finished its tea, and you do it cleanly. People trust the pairing of a practised hand and a quick spirit, and they come to you when something has to be mended today.","Impatience can pass for high standards, so the first flash of frustration lands on a detail instead of the real cause. The Sun then holds that position stubbornly. You may correct a person when you meant to say you are tired. Growth is naming the feeling before fixing the thing."],"taurus-aries-libra":["Why does being fair take so long, when I could simply decide? You ask it with a smile, usually while pouring tea for two people who disagree. The Libra Rising is the smile: gracious, symmetrical, quick to make everyone comfortable. The Aries Moon, directly opposite, is the question. It wants a verdict, an action, a door opened with a bang. The Taurus Sun, Venus-ruled and unhurried, stands in the middle and holds the teapot.","Aries Moon and Libra Rising are opposite, so what you need and how you appear lean on each other like two ends of a seesaw: directness against diplomacy, the self against the other. Venus rules both the Taurus Sun and the Libra Rising, but they sit five signs apart, so the shared taste for beauty and ease has to be adjusted all the time to fit. The Sun mostly keeps the peace by being sensual and unhurried, which gives the Moon time to cool.","Fair play with a pulse. You can say the direct thing graciously, mediate while knowing what you want yourself, and enjoy a good argument without losing the friendship. People trust you because you are plainly kind and plainly capable of anger, so your kindness is a choice.","The Rising charms the room into peace while the Moon wants a fight, so the anger leaks out sideways as sarcasm or a sudden cold withdrawal. The Sun digs in to avoid a scene. Growth is saying the Aries sentence once, early and warmly, and finding that the friendship holds."],"taurus-aries-scorpio":["At fifty you will understand what at twenty only embarrassed you: the flash of Aries temper was never the trouble, the guarded face that followed it was. The Scorpio Rising watches the room with an unreadable calm, while the Aries Moon wants to say it now and clear the air. The Taurus Sun is the river stone in all this, unhurried and hard to move. Strangers meet the stillness. The people closest to you meet the weather.","Your Sun and Rising face each other across the wheel, both fixed, so the self you are building and the face you wear lean on one another like a seesaw: comfort and constancy against intensity and secrecy. The Aries Moon is a neighbour to the Sun and a stranger to the Rising, so the need to react quickly never quite meets the gaze that withholds. Mars rules both Moon and Rising, which is why the stillness is charged and the temper arrives fast. Calm here is a held breath, and it improves when you exhale on purpose.","Courage with a long fuse after it. You can start the difficult conversation, hold the room through the silence that follows, and still be there the next morning. People trust you in a crisis because you move quickly and then, unusually, stay. Your loyalty is physical: you arrive with the van, the soup and the spare key.","The Moon wants to discharge and the Rising wants to guard, so anger may be swallowed on Tuesday and delivered, whole and unrecognisable, the following month. The Sun then digs in, because being asked to explain itself feels like being dragged. Growth is saying the small hot sentence the same day, in a plain voice, before it has time to become a case."],"taurus-aries-sagittarius":["You are in a tearing hurry and in no hurry at all, and both are true by lunchtime. The Sagittarius Rising arrives with news, a laugh and a half-formed plan for the weekend. The Aries Moon wants to start it today with whoever is nearest. Your Sun in Taurus lets the first rush go past, checks the budget, then sets about doing it properly and keeps doing it for years. Friends see a flame that lights quickly. The result is a fire that holds.","Two fire lights and one earth. The Aries Moon and the Sagittarius Rising are a trine, so need and manner agree and move together, quickly and with some joy. The Sun is next door to the Moon and has little in common with the Rising, so it is the one that has to translate the fire into something that lasts. Mars drives the Moon and Jupiter the Rising, which makes enthusiasm easy and follow-through your real achievement. You are at your best when the Sun sets the pace of the second week.","Momentum that survives the first week. You start with courage, speak with warmth, and stay with a project long enough for the early excitement to become a skill. People follow you because you are decisive and generous, and because you are still around when the work gets dull.","Two lights want the open road, so a decision can be made quickly and defended slowly, with the Sun refusing to admit it was rushed. Impatience gets called honesty and stubbornness gets called principle. Growth is letting one night pass between the impulse and the commitment, and letting someone you trust ask the awkward question in that gap."],"taurus-aries-capricorn":["The impatience lives in your right hand, which wants to do something now, and the composure lives in your spine, which will not allow it. The Capricorn Rising meets the world dry-witted, upright and apparently older than the calendar. The Aries Moon is the pulse under it, quick to feel and quick to want. Your Sun in Taurus sides with the long game and a fire that lasts the whole winter. People see someone unflappable. Those near you learn the signs that the fuse is lit.","Taurus Sun and Capricorn Rising are both earth and in trine, so what you are and how you appear support each other with very little friction: solid, unhurried, built to last. The Aries Moon squares the Rising, both cardinal, so the need to react and the discipline to hold back meet at a right angle, and that is where the pressure builds. Mars and Saturn do not speak the same language. When the Sun takes the Moon’s urgency and gives it a schedule, the pressure becomes drive.","Driven reliability. You take responsibility without being asked, you protect those who depend on you, and you have the courage to say the hard thing early, in a level voice. You can begin quickly, carry on through the dull middle and finish what you began.","The Moon wants to explode and the Rising wants to behave, so anger can arrive as sarcasm or sit as a headache. The Sun holds its line long after the argument is over. Growth is letting the heat be visible while it is small, and letting people see that the dry manner has a pulse."],"taurus-aries-aquarius":["The first stroke of a brush on a blank wall: one decisive line, made before anyone agreed what the picture would be. That is how you begin things. The Aries Moon makes the line, because waiting is the one thing it cannot bear. The Aquarius Rising explains the picture to the room, cheerfully and from a slight distance, as though it were already on the wall. Your Sun in Taurus is the one who stays afterwards to finish the job, in the same colour, all the way to the corner.","The Taurus Sun squares the Aquarius Rising, both fixed, so the self you are building and the manner you present argue about the same thing: tradition against novelty, comfort against being ahead of the curve. The Aries Moon is a friendly sextile from the Rising, so impulse and originality cooperate easily, and it is only the Sun that has to be persuaded. Three different elements make the chart varied rather than harmonious. Expect to be asked why you are so calm about plans that sound so strange.","Courageous originality. You say the unfashionable thing early and then do the patient work that proves it. You are friendly without being clingy, direct without being cruel, and unusually good at making a new idea feel safe enough to try.","The Moon wants to act now, the Rising wants to be unusual and the Sun wants not to be pushed, so a bold start can be followed by a long, stubborn refusal to adjust. Cool manners cover a short temper. Growth is letting a trusted friend edit the plan after the first stroke, and letting some of the edits stay."],"taurus-aries-pisces":["Is it allowed to want to go first and to disappear in the same afternoon? You ask it half-aloud, usually while standing in a doorway. The Pisces Rising meets the world softly, with a faraway look and a gentleness people project their hopes onto. The Aries Moon is the ram on the high ledge, needing action, a fast answer and a way to spend the day’s feeling. The Sun in Taurus lies between them, sensory, unhurried and determined to finish the meal. You seem dreamy until someone blocks the path.","These are three neighbouring signs: Pisces Rising, Aries Moon and Taurus Sun run in a row round the wheel, each a single step from the next, so each light barely sees the one beyond it. Sun and Rising are a friendly sextile, so comfort and gentleness cooperate easily. The Moon, the only fire, stays apart: its fast, clean feelings arrive without introduction in a face built for fog. Jupiter and Neptune rule the Rising, which blurs the edge of what Mars needs.","Soft power. You can move people without pushing them, start something with real courage and still make it feel like a gift. You combine intuition with a very practical hand, and your presence calms rooms that would otherwise argue.","The Moon wants to strike and the Rising wants not to cause a fuss, so anger leaves as a sigh, a late arrival or a tearful retreat. The Sun then holds its ground out of sight. Growth is saying the plain, fast sentence while the feeling is still clean, and trusting that gentleness survives it."],"taurus-taurus-aries":["You arrive at a trot, claim the best chair and are not moved from it for three hours. Strangers meet the Aries Rising: brisk, direct, a little impatient, someone who wants an answer by Friday. Friends meet the rest. You keep routines, one good mug and a standing order for the bread you like, and your body unclenches only when the evening is arranged. Hurry you and you go quiet. Hurry you when you are tired and you become a gatepost with opinions.","Sun and Moon share Taurus, and the Moon is exalted there, so identity and need agree: comfort, loyalty, things that last. Both are fixed and Venus rules both, which gives a calm that is hard to argue with. The Aries Rising stands one sign back from each, a semi-sextile, and is the only light that wants to hurry. It sets the pace at the door, then discovers that the two lights behind it will not move until they are ready. You are fast to enter and slow to be shifted.","Staying power with a pulse. You are the one who begins the project and the one still there, with snacks, when it ends. Your appetite for good things is catching, you are hard to flatter and harder to scare, and your loyalty turns up with a casserole and a toolbox. Your calm is not a pose; the body really works that way.","Two fixed lights can turn a preference into a monument, and the brisk Aries front makes the refusal sound like a decision rather than a habit. You may defend a routine long after it has stopped feeding you, and take any change as an insult. Growth is saying yes to one small disruption a month, and noticing that the ground held."],"taurus-taurus-taurus":["Three housemates share one table. The Sun keeps the accounts and wants whatever you build to last. The Moon wants soup, a warm blanket and the same chair as yesterday. The Rising answers the door, unhurried, and decides who comes in. Visitors meet the one at the door and assume the house is as simple as its welcome. You are rarely rattled, you keep promises with your whole body, and you change direction about once a decade, after long thought and a very good meal.","All three lights share Taurus, so nobody inside you argues about what matters, only about timing. The Moon is exalted here, an honoured guest, which makes your needs unusually legible to you: you know when you are hungry, tired or finished. With no angle between the lights there is also no outside view. Nothing in the chart interrupts a habit, so a habit slowly becomes a law. Venus rules all of it and sets one tempo: pleasure first, never rushed.","Reliability that people can lean their whole weight on. You are consistent in mood, generous with food and company, and exceptionally hard to panic. You build things that last, you sense what a room needs to feel safe, and your word, once given, works like infrastructure.","Nothing in you objects, so rigidity can pass for character. You may keep a routine long after it has stopped feeding you, or refuse a change simply because it arrived too fast. Comfort becomes a fortress. Growth is borrowing a stranger’s opinion on purpose, once a season, and letting one small habit be wrong."],"taurus-taurus-gemini":["You stand at the front door with your coat on and a hand on the latch, and twenty minutes later you are still finishing the story you began on the step. People see someone brisk, amused and about to leave. The coat is a formality. Taurus holds both your Sun and your Moon, and both want the sofa, the second helping, the same table at the same cafe each Thursday. The chatter is how you enjoy the room, not how you escape it.","Sun and Moon share Taurus, and the Moon is exalted there, so purpose and need speak one language: appetite, comfort and loyalty arrive without an argument. Only the Gemini Rising stands apart, a semi-sextile neighbour to both, close and slightly out of view. Mercury rules the surface and Venus the core, so you describe sensations more often than you chase whims. This chart lacks a second opinion, and the speed of the face can pass for one.","Comfort that talks back. You make a room feel fed in every sense and keep a friendship alive for years with small, accurate remembering. You are reliable without being dull and funny without being flighty, and you can describe a pleasure so well that other people finally allow themselves to have it.","When Sun and Moon agree, a habit can become so complete that only a crisis reveals it was a habit. Talk can stand in for change: you describe the new plan beautifully and keep the old routine. Growth is letting one small thing be different on purpose, then noticing that you survived it."],"taurus-taurus-cancer":["People take the gentle manner for a gentle will, and they learn otherwise the first time someone suggests moving the dining table. The Cancer Rising offers a welcome, a second helping, a memory for who takes sugar. Behind it, the Taurus Sun and the Taurus Moon agree about nearly everything: what is good, what is yours, what is not up for discussion. You are kind to people and immovable about arrangements, and you see no contradiction at all.","Sun and Moon share Taurus, and the Moon is exalted there, so what you want and what you need speak one language with almost no friction. That is a gift and a blind spot, because nobody inside the chart disagrees and a decision can harden without ever being examined. The Cancer Rising is a sextile to both lights, which gives the pair a gracious front and a good ear for how others feel. The ear mostly reports whether people are comfortable. It rarely asks whether the plan should change.","Permanence you can lean on. You remember preferences, keep promises for decades, and turn food, fabric and routine into something people rest against. You are hard to rush and impossible to bribe, and the people close to you know where you stand, and that it will still be true next year.","Comfort can become a verdict. You may keep a chair, a habit or a grievance long after it has stopped serving anyone, and defend it by being kind about it, which makes it harder for others to argue. Change feels like a small bereavement. Growth is moving one thing on purpose each season and noticing that you survived it."],"taurus-taurus-leo":["The best minute of your evening is the one after the last guest leaves, when the music is off and so are the shoes. Until then you were the warm, slightly grand host the Leo Rising promises, and you meant every toast. The Taurus Sun and Moon share a sign and agree on nearly everything: good food, a routine that belongs to you, a chair that fits. The performance is real. It is an outing from a settled life.","All three lights are fixed, so nothing in this chart moves unless it wants to. Sun and Moon share Taurus, which means what you are and what you need speak one language: pleasure that lasts and worth you can count. Leo Rising squares both, fire against earth, and that single angle is the whole drama. The front wants to be seen and applauded. The pair behind it want to be left comfortable. You resolve it by being generous in public on a budget set in private.","Reliability with warmth. You turn up, you remember the occasion, and the present you chose is the one still in use ten years later. People feel looked after by someone who is also good company, and that combination is rarer than it sounds.","Fixed on every side, you can hold an opinion, a grievance or a favourite chair long past its usefulness, and defend it so graciously that no one sees the lock. Being praised for steadiness can keep you steady when you need to move. Growth is changing one small habit on purpose, before life changes it for you."],"taurus-taurus-virgo":["You tidy when you are tired and call it resting. The Virgo Rising has you folding towels while the evening ends, and the Taurus Sun and Moon, sharing one sign, would honestly prefer a sofa and something good to eat. People see a capable, quiet, well-kept person who has things in order. They rarely see how much of that order is a way of making a comfortable life, and how much you simply enjoy it.","All three lights are earth, and Sun and Moon both trine the Rising, so there is hardly any friction here, which is its own challenge. Sun and Moon share Taurus, so what you are and what you need speak with one voice: pleasure, steadiness, things that last. The Virgo Rising adds the habit of improving whatever it touches. Mercury rules it, so the mind is a careful and practical tool. The risk is a chart so agreeable with itself that nothing disturbs it into change.","Craft you can live inside. You make a home, a garden, a meal or a spreadsheet that works every day and looks good doing it. You are unflashy and extremely dependable, and your standards are generous enough that people feel looked after rather than inspected.","Everything agrees, so nothing pushes, and you can drift through years of comfortable maintenance without asking whether you want something different. A small habit hardens into a rule. Growth is choosing one thing a year that is a little uncomfortable on purpose."],"taurus-taurus-libra":["Three voices share one table. The Libra Rising stands at the salon door with a welcome and an eye for who feels left out. The Taurus Moon is in the kitchen, plain and certain, already wanting the plates warm and the evening slow. The Taurus Sun agrees with the Moon about everything and sits at the head of the table without mentioning that it will not leave before the second helping.","Sun and Moon share Taurus and speak one language: comfort, loyalty, a table worth sitting at. The Libra Rising stands five signs from both, so the face you wear never quite matches the feeling behind it, though Venus rules all three signs and keeps the taste consistent. The effect is someone easy to like and hard to move. The Rising negotiates. The pair behind it simply stays.","Hospitality with backbone. You make people feel welcome and then keep the promise implied by the welcome. You are fair, warm and reliable, and your sense of beauty shows in the table, the garden and the way you speak to waiters.","Your pleasantness can be mistaken for flexibility, so people find out where the line is only by crossing it. Moon and Sun both dig in, and the Rising smiles throughout. Growth is saying “no, and here is why” before the third time something has been moved."],"taurus-taurus-scorpio":["At a party you take the chair with its back to the wall, and within a quarter of an hour someone is telling you what they meant to keep to themselves. The Scorpio Rising does that, with a level gaze and a charged stillness. Sun and Moon in Taurus want the opposite: soup, a good chair, a long evening and nobody asking for a decision. So the room sees a locked door, and behind it you are mostly checking whether the bread has risen.","Sun and Moon share Taurus, so what you are and what you need speak one language: comfort, constancy, a body at ease. The Scorpio Rising stands opposite both, and all three signs are fixed, so the seesaw has no give. Everything you present is more intense than anything you feel, and the intensity is borrowed from a Rising that watches for betrayal the Taurus lights would rather not imagine. With no outside voice among the lights, the main difficulty is that nobody inside you ever says “perhaps”.","Reliability that people can lean their whole weight on. You see who is lying quickly and make a scene about it slowly, so you protect people without announcing it. Your loyalty has seasons, your appetite for life is real, and your calm in an emergency comes from having already decided to stay.","With two lights in the same sign you are right in a very comfortable way, and the Rising treats a changed mind as a breach. A grievance can sit in the cellar for years, fed regularly and never mentioned. Growth is letting a trusted person watch you be unsure, and finding that being seen mid-decision does not cost you your footing."],"taurus-taurus-sagittarius":["People see the easy laugh and the open door and assume you will be gone by autumn. They have misread the weather. The Sagittarius Rising is the hospitality, the news from elsewhere and the invitation, and it is entirely sincere. But Sun and Moon both sit in Taurus, and they plan to be in this house, with this table and these people, for a very long time. You welcome travellers and keep the lamp lit for them. Anyone who has watched you for a year knows you will still be here.","Sun and Moon share Taurus, so your aim and your appetite are one voice, devoted to comfort, constancy and good things done well. The Sagittarius Rising sits out of step with both, sharing neither element nor mode, so the face you wear is always a little more adventurous than the life you actually build. That gap is productive: it brings the world to a doorstep that never moves. Jupiter rules the Rising, so the generosity is real, and the exalted Moon keeps it affordable.","Hospitality with roots. You make a settled life feel open to the world, and you are generous in ways that can be counted on: the meal, the loan, the spare room. You are good at long friendships, long projects and the kind of faith that is practised rather than announced.","A doubled sign makes comfort very persuasive. The Rising talks about new horizons while Sun and Moon quietly veto each one, so you can feel more adventurous than your calendar shows. Growth is accepting one invitation a season that the Taurus lights would not choose, and staying long enough to find out whether you liked it."],"taurus-taurus-capricorn":["At seven in the evening, when the work is done, the kitchen is warm and nobody needs anything, you finally exhale. Sun and Moon in Taurus ask for the same things: good food, a settled routine, a body at ease and a place that belongs to you. The Capricorn Rising adds the face that gets it all organised: serious, capable, dry-humoured and a little hard to impress. People rely on you quickly. They take longer to learn how much you enjoy things.","All three lights are earth, and Sun and Moon share Taurus, so the self, the need and the manner agree about nearly everything: build slowly, save carefully, keep what is good. The Capricorn Rising is in trine with both, so what you show is an easy extension of what you are. It is a coherent arrangement with no outside view, and nobody inside you ever suggests a change of plan. Saturn rules the Rising and gives the comfort a conscience.","Reliability you can build a house on. You are generous in practical ways, quick to repair, hard to shake and good at turning a fragile idea into an object that lasts. People feel safe near you for good reason, and your private pleasures are quietly infectious: food, music, a well-made tool.","A coherent chart has no objector. Routine becomes a fortress, comfort becomes an argument against any change, and the dry manner hides how much you would like to be surprised. Growth is scheduling something unplanned, with someone you like, and letting it be a little inconvenient."],"taurus-taurus-aquarius":["When pushed, you do not argue. You become more yourself, calmly, and a little stranger, until the other party gives up. Sun and Moon both sit in Taurus, so your purpose and your comfort agree to the point of obstinacy: good food, a settled day, loyalty and no surprises. The Aquarius Rising puts a very different face on it: friendly, unusual and slightly ahead of the room. People think you are a free spirit. You think you are a person with a very particular routine.","Sun and Moon share Taurus, so the self and the need speak with one stubborn voice, and the Aquarius Rising squares both, so friction between them and your outer manner is built into every first impression. All three signs are fixed. You look like an experiment and behave like an institution. The Moon is exalted and keeps the peace at home, while the Rising keeps the neighbours guessing.","Stability with a surprise in it. You are loyal, sensual and calm, yet your ideas about how to live are unconventional enough to inspire people. You can keep a promise for thirty years and a joke for longer, and your home is often the most interesting room in the street.","Fixed on every side, you can mistake a rut for a principle and an eccentricity for a position. The Rising explains the stubbornness so charmingly that it goes unexamined. Growth is changing one habit a year for no better reason than curiosity, and noticing that the world does not end."],"taurus-taurus-pisces":["Two of you sit at the kitchen table with your elbows on it, agreeing that supper should be good and that nobody should rush it. The third stands at the window, watching the rain, wondering whether supper could also be a poem. Sun and Moon in Taurus ask for comfort, repetition and a body at ease. The Pisces Rising meets the world gently, with a faraway look and a way of making people feel unhurried. Visitors meet the window. Family meets the table.","Sun and Moon share Taurus, so the self and the need are one steady voice, and the Pisces Rising makes a friendly sextile with both. Your purpose and your comfort are practical and sensual, and the way you appear is soft and receptive, so the chart is unusually free of friction. The Moon is exalted, which makes comfort feel like grace. The only difficulty is that nobody inside you ever disagrees, so change tends to arrive from outside.","Restful presence. You make people feel that nothing is urgent, that the soup is hot and the world will wait. You are loyal, tactile and quietly artistic, and you have a feeling for the kind of kindness that never asks to be thanked.","Comfort is so persuasive, and the Rising so agreeable, that nothing ever gets decided. Avoidance wears the face of peace. The Sun stands firm on the small things and goes vague on the large ones. Growth is making the one uncomfortable decision that has been waiting by the door, and trusting that the soup will still be hot."],"taurus-gemini-aries":["What happens next, and who can I tell first? That is the question under your whole day, and you ask it at a brisk walk. People meet the Aries Rising: direct, laughing before the sentence ends, already half out of the chair. What they miss is the Gemini Moon’s appetite for a new topic every hour, and the Taurus Sun’s insistence that each new topic arrive with a snack and a seat. You hoard facts like jars, and serve them in the order they occurred to you.","Gemini Moon and Aries Rising sit in a sextile, a friendly angle between air and fire, so talk feeds action and action gives talk something to report. That pair is quick, curious and slightly breathless. Your Taurus Sun is one sign from each and sees both only dimly, so it keeps asking for a fuller, slower version of whatever the other two have already finished. Mercury, which rules the Moon, wants variety; Venus, which rules the Sun, wants depth. They settle it by turning a hobby into a collection.","Learning that sticks. You pick up a skill in an afternoon and, because of the Taurus Sun, you actually keep it. You can explain without condescending, talk to anyone in a queue, and rescue a flat evening by wanting to know what happens next. Your humour is physical and warm, and you remember what people told you three months ago.","You can describe a feeling so well that you never get round to having it, and the Aries front makes the narration sound like decisiveness. Interests multiply, then sit half-finished, which stings the part of you that loves completion. Growth is an hour a day with no screen and no listener, long enough to hear what the Moon says once it stops talking."],"taurus-gemini-taurus":["At fifty you may stop believing you had to choose. The person who stays put and the person who wonders were one guest all along. For now you look unhurried: the low voice, the armchair, the plate someone has already filled. Meanwhile the Gemini Moon is on its fourth topic, with two books open and a friend you intend to ring at nine. Stillness without ideas feels like a locked room to you. People see contentment, and it is real, but it comes with a very busy head.","Venus rules your Sun and Rising, and both want one good thing at a time, fully enjoyed. Mercury rules your Moon, and it wants all the things at once. The Gemini Moon sits one sign from each Taurus light, close enough to share a wall and not a language. The result is a familiar comedy. Your head signs you up for the whole week and your body declines to attend. Over the years the two learn to take turns, and the evenings improve.","Conversation that feeds people. You are calm enough that anyone can think aloud near you, and quick enough to find the sentence they were reaching for. You explain things simply, remember who said what, and make learning feel like an afternoon rather than a chore. You can carry a long project and still enjoy the detours.","You may talk about a feeling in place of having it, and the unhurried manner lets the dodge pass as composure. The week fills with curiosities, then you resent the schedule you wrote. Growth is one unfilled evening with a chair and no audience, long enough for the Moon to finish a thought that has no use."],"taurus-gemini-gemini":["You want nothing to change and you cannot stop changing the subject. The Taurus Sun asks for the same chair, the same street and the dinner it had last Tuesday. Two lights out of three are Gemini, and they ask for a fresh question every ten minutes. Neither side is lying. You have found a way to be settled while in motion: the same table, a different conversation each time. Strangers meet the talker, and the friends who last find the table.","Moon and Rising both stand in Gemini, so what you feel and how you appear move at one speed. Mercury rules both, which means feeling arrives as language and is named almost as it happens. The Taurus Sun is a neighbouring sign to each and cannot quite see them, a semi-sextile, which is why its slow tastes can startle the talk. Fixed meets mutable here. Mercury sets the weather and Venus keeps the larder.","Making the familiar interesting. You can sit in one place for years and keep finding new things to say about it, which is why you are so good at long friendships, long projects and long dinners. You learn fast, translate gracefully between people, and keep a home that is also a good conversation.","Moon and Rising agree, so nothing in you slows the talk down. You may name a feeling exactly and leave it there, as if the label were the care. The Sun can dig in on a view you stated lightly. Growth is staying quiet with one feeling until it has changed shape by itself."],"taurus-gemini-cancer":["A feeling lands in your throat and hands before it lands anywhere else. You fold your arms loosely over your middle, a posture that reads as comfort and works as a gate, and you begin to talk. People meet the Cancer Rising: attentive, a little protective, easy to confide in. What they do not see is that you narrate yourself in order to find out what is going on. By the third retelling you know, and the Taurus Sun has quietly decided what to do about it.","Three neighbouring signs make a staircase: Taurus, Gemini, Cancer. Each light sees clearly only the one next to it, so the Gemini Moon in the middle must translate between a Sun that wants to stay put and a Rising that wants to shelter. Sun and Rising are a sextile apart and cooperate when asked. The Moon is the restless, verbal one, and because it rules your Rising it also sets your moods, which can change by the hour.","Comfort that talks back. You can make a tense table laugh, put a hard feeling into words others can use, and remember the small details that prove you were listening. You are practical about what you say you will do, and people feel that their stories have somewhere safe to land.","Talking can stand in for feeling. You may describe the hurt thoroughly to three friends and never once to the person who caused it, and the Cancer front then holds a mood the Gemini Moon has already explained away. Growth is sitting one full evening in silence with a feeling, and letting the body finish its sentence before the mouth does."],"taurus-gemini-leo":["A millstone grinds slowly and rattles the whole time, which is a fair picture of you in company. The Leo Rising warms the room and holds the floor, the Gemini Moon keeps a running commentary in the margins, and the Taurus Sun goes on with the real work at its own pace. People see someone sociable, funny, a little theatrical. They do not always see you quietly deciding what is worth keeping.","Taurus and Gemini are neighbours, so Sun and Moon barely follow each other: one trusts what lasts, the other collects what is new. Leo Rising sextiles the Moon, an easy angle, and hands all those ideas a stage and an audience. It squares the Sun, so the friction lives between being admired and being settled. The result is a mind that jokes freely and a will that decides slowly, with the joke sometimes arriving before the decision.","Charm with follow-through. You can talk to anyone, keep a conversation alive and then do the thing you promised on Tuesday. You explain what you know with warmth and plain examples, and you make learning feel like a good meal shared.","Talk can stand in for feeling, so you may narrate a hurt in a funny voice and never reach what it was. Meanwhile the Sun digs in around the one subject you will not discuss. Growth is saying the unstyled sentence once, without the joke, and noticing who stays to hear it."],"taurus-gemini-virgo":["Have I said that clearly, or only correctly? You ask it at six in the morning at a clean desk, rereading the message you sent last night. The Virgo Rising presents a tidy, careful, helpful person. The Gemini Moon is the reason for the rereading: a mind that feels by naming and cannot rest until the word fits. The Sun is the part that finally presses send and goes to eat bread.","Mercury rules both the Gemini Moon and the Virgo Rising, so mind and manner share one planet and one language: precise, quick to notice, fond of lists. The two square each other, both mutable, so the same fluency turns into second-guessing. The Taurus Sun backs the Rising with an easy trine and sits beside the Moon without quite following her. It stands with the practical half of you. You are most at ease when a thought can become something finished and useful.","Clear, useful words. You explain complicated things in the right order, edit gracefully and notice what was left out of the plan. People bring you drafts, questions and tangled instructions because you will return them cleaner and kinder than you found them.","With Mercury on both sides the mind rarely rests, and worry can masquerade as diligence. You may revise a message until the feeling in it is gone. The Sun, practical and stubborn, can then refuse to change a plan the mind has already seen the flaw in. Growth is sending the imperfect version and letting it be read."],"taurus-gemini-libra":["By fifty you will know which conversations were worth having, and you will have had most of the others anyway, with great charm. For now the Libra Rising makes you gracious and quick to find common ground, and the Gemini Moon keeps the line humming with questions, jokes and half-finished ideas. The Taurus Sun is the pole that holds the wire up: calm, steady and a little amused.","Libra Rising and the Gemini Moon are both air and trine, so the face you wear and the mind you need agree with almost no effort: talk, company and a fair hearing. The Sun is the odd one. It stands one sign from the Moon and five from the Rising, so what you are building sees neither the chatter nor the grace clearly. Venus rules Sun and Rising, so the pleasure in beauty and kindness stays steady behind the wit.","Ease with people. You can talk to a stranger, a child or a difficult relative and leave each of them feeling heard. You draw connections between people as readily as between ideas, and your friendships are many and surprisingly durable.","Because so much comes easily to Rising and Moon, the Sun can be left to do the slow work alone, and attention spreads across a dozen agreeable conversations while few things get finished. Growth is choosing one project that deserves silence and giving it a season."],"taurus-gemini-scorpio":["You talk constantly and tell almost nothing, and both are sincere. The Gemini Moon thinks by speaking, so questions, jokes and half-formed theories pour out of you all day. The Scorpio Rising decides what any of it may reveal, which is why a stranger hears a lively friend and an old friend hears one true sentence a year. Your Taurus Sun stays out of the argument, wanting a good meal, a reliable income and nobody pressing it for answers.","Taurus Sun and Gemini Moon are neighbours, so your will and your instincts hardly see each other: one wants things to stay, the other wants to know what else there is. The Scorpio Rising opposes the Sun and sits at a slant to the Moon, so the face you wear has never been properly introduced to the voice you think in. Three different elements make a workshop with three doors. The Sun is the only light that stays put, and the others keep borrowing its table.","A mind that can hold both a spreadsheet and a secret. You listen precisely, remember what was said and what was nearly said, and ask the question one level lower than the one people expected. You are good at negotiations, interviews, diagnoses and any conversation where the real subject is not the stated one.","Talk can become the screen: you give a hundred accurate details to avoid giving one vulnerable one. The Sun then holds whatever position was stated last, and the Rising files whatever was not. Growth is finishing a sentence that begins with “I feel” without turning it into an observation about someone else."],"taurus-gemini-sagittarius":["The feeling arrives in your throat and your feet at once: a queue of words, and a pair of legs that want to be somewhere else. The Gemini Moon needs to talk it through with someone quick. The Sagittarius Rising opposite it turns that talk into a trip, a theory or a punchline. Your Taurus Sun rests its elbows on the table and would like both of them to sit down for lunch. You are good company, hard to pin down, and surprisingly firm about the few things that matter.","Gemini Moon and Sagittarius Rising face each other across the wheel, both mutable, so the mind you think with and the face you show pull like a seesaw: detail and curiosity against faith and the big picture. The Taurus Sun is a neighbour of the Moon and a stranger to the Rising, which makes it the only light with a fixed address. It anchors the argument. The result is someone who can follow any conversation and still, by evening, wants the table laid.","Quick learning with a lasting memory. You collect stories, languages, shortcuts and contacts, then turn them into something useful and well made. People enjoy your company, rely on your word and find that your enthusiasm comes with a plan for dinner.","Moon and Rising keep each other busy, so you can scatter yourself across ten interesting things while the Sun waits to be asked what matters. Opinions get held loudly and examined late. Growth is a quiet hour with no input, in which you find out which of the ten you would still choose."],"taurus-gemini-capricorn":["An old ledger with its margins crowded: neat columns in the middle, and around them, in smaller and faster handwriting, jokes, questions and half-finished ideas. That is you. The Capricorn Rising keeps the columns: composed, dry and apparently unhurried. The Gemini Moon fills the margins, needing talk, news and a person quick enough to answer. Your Taurus Sun decides which of the notes becomes a plan. You seem serious until you are comfortable, and then you are the funniest person at the table.","Taurus Sun and Capricorn Rising are both earth and in trine, so what you are and how you appear agree: solid, reliable, built to last. The Gemini Moon is the odd one out. It sits next door to the Sun and out of step with the Rising, so the need for talk, variety and ideas rarely matches the reserved face you present. Two earth lights holding an air Moon feels like a library with the windows open. Mercury and Saturn cooperate when the work is interesting.","Disciplined curiosity. You learn quickly and retain what you learn, you write or explain with dry precision, and you can make a complicated subject usable. People trust your judgement because it is evidently built from a lot of reading and a little scepticism.","The mind runs on the Moon’s schedule and the face runs on the Rising’s, so you may look calm while thinking in six directions, and nobody knows to offer help. The Sun holds each opinion longer than the evidence warrants. Growth is saying the half-formed thought aloud to someone you trust, before it hardens into a position."],"taurus-gemini-aquarius":["Who else is thinking this, and can they come round for dinner? You ask it constantly, usually aloud. The Gemini Moon needs a quick mind to talk to, and the Aquarius Rising, in an easy trine with it, supplies a face that is friendly, curious and ready for anyone with an unusual idea. Your Taurus Sun has other plans: a settled evening, a good meal and one conversation properly finished. So you collect people, and then you cook for them.","Two air lights and one earth. Gemini Moon and Aquarius Rising are a trine, so need and manner flow together: curious, talkative, a little detached. The Taurus Sun squares the Rising, so the part of you that wants comfort and constancy argues with the part that wants to be ahead of the conversation, and it barely sees the Moon next door at all. The effect is easy company around a slow centre.","Friendly intelligence. You make connections between people and ideas, explain the unusual so that it sounds sensible, and keep the conversation moving without losing the thread. You are generous with introductions and unexpectedly dependable for someone so interested in everything.","Talk and ideas make a comfortable cloud. You can live in the exchange of opinions and leave the body’s needs unattended: sleep, a proper meal, a decision. The Sun then retreats into stubbornness when pressed. Growth is closing a loop with a person or a task before opening the next conversation."],"taurus-gemini-pisces":["By fifty you will understand that you were never indecisive. You were holding two true things at once, and the world kept asking you to drop one. The Gemini Moon thinks and feels by talking, so it keeps a dozen questions in the air. The Pisces Rising squares it, and softens the dozen into a mood, a drift, a look that seems to be listening to something far away. Your Sun in Taurus supports the Rising and wants only a good meal, a clear hour and one thing finished.","Gemini Moon and Pisces Rising are a square, both mutable, so the quick mind and the porous face keep crossing: one wants to name what it feels, the other to dissolve in it. The Taurus Sun is a friendly sextile to the Rising and next door to the Moon, so it sides with the water while barely seeing the talker beside it. The three share no element. Jupiter and Neptune rule the Rising, so the mood is generous and a little foggy, and Mercury has to check the map.","Imaginative fluency. You find words for what other people only feel, you make a story out of a mood and a mood out of a story, and you can talk with a stranger as if you were old friends. You are a natural translator between the practical and the poetic.","Mind and mood keep each other busy, so you may explain a feeling instead of having it, or have a feeling and call it a theory. The Sun leans on comfort when the question is hard. Growth is a quiet hour with no talk and no screen, to see what the water says when the words have stopped."],"taurus-cancer-aries":["Three residents share your house. The Aries Rising is at the door with its boots already on, asking what that noise was. The Cancer Moon is in the kitchen, counting who has eaten and who has not called. The Taurus Sun sits in the best chair and will not be hurried by either. Visitors only see the one at the door: protective, quick, ready to fight for whoever is inside. What they miss is how much of you lives in the kitchen.","The Cancer Moon is at home in its own sign, so feeling runs fluent and strong, and it squares your Aries Rising. Both are cardinal and both want to begin, but one starts a fight and the other starts a pot of soup. Your Taurus Sun sextiles the Moon, so comfort and care agree about almost everything, and the household stays fed. The door guard usually wins the first move; the kitchen wins the second. When the square eases, worry comes out as action rather than irritation.","Protection that works. You see trouble coming early, move before the discussion and then feed whoever you rescued. Care arrives in practical forms: a repaired lock, a full fridge, a firm call to the landlord. You are brave on behalf of others, calm when the roof leaks, and a long keeper of recipes, names and old kindnesses.","Fear for your people can come out as sharpness, and a clipped word at the door lands on someone who only wanted to help. You may hide a hurt behind a project, then resent that nobody asked. Growth is carrying the kitchen’s truth into the front room and saying it plainly: I was frightened, not angry."],"taurus-cancer-taurus":["At the door of someone else’s kitchen, coat still on, you are already rinsing a mug. It is a small gesture and it says everything: you notice who is tired, who has not eaten, who has gone quiet at the edge of the room. The Taurus presence makes this look like ordinary good manners. The Cancer Moon knows better. It keeps the birthdays, the favourite biscuits and the names of everyone’s worries, and it wants, more than it will say, to be remembered back.","The Cancer Moon is at home in its own sign and sextile to both Taurus lights, so water and earth cooperate: the Moon supplies the feeling and Taurus supplies the pots, the pantry and the patience to follow through. Little in you fights itself. The weakness of such ease is that no one has to ask for anything. The Moon waits to be noticed and the Taurus pair waits to be asked, and a need can sit for months in a perfectly warm house.","Shelter that does not announce itself. You feed, remember and show up, and you have the memory for what each person likes and the calm to make it. People feel held around you without feeling managed. You guard a household’s peace, mark its anniversaries and keep a spare bed made.","Care can become a way of asking: you give a great deal and wait, in silence, to be given back to. Hurt goes into the pantry with the other stores and returns months later as a chill. Growth is saying “I need this” while the kettle is still hot, before the silence says it for you."],"taurus-cancer-gemini":["People usually decide you are light. You joke easily, talk with your hands, and ask a stranger in a lift three bright questions. They conclude that you do not hold on to things. Nearly the reverse is true. You remember birthdays, allergies, who was ill in March and who left a party early looking pale. The chatter is a form of tending, and the Cancer Moon keeps the real accounts in a cupboard no visitor ever sees.","The Taurus Sun sextiles the Cancer Moon, earth and water, so wanting to provide and needing to be held fit together when you let them. The Moon is in its own sign and feels without friction. Gemini Rising sits one sign from each and speaks another language, a semi-sextile, so the surface cannot quite translate the feeling it fronts. Mercury makes you articulate about everything except what you need most, which tends to come out as a question about someone else’s evening.","Care that is also entertaining. You feed people, remember them and look after them, and you make them laugh while you do it, which is why they accept the help. You are good with the frightened, the grieving and the shy, because you can speak lightly to them without leaving them alone.","You may answer a question about yourself with one about the asker, so your own needs stay unspoken until they are heavy. The Sun can then dig in over a small matter that is standing in for a large one. Growth is offering one direct, unfunny sentence, “I would like to be looked after tonight”, and letting it land."],"taurus-cancer-cancer":["Ten minutes after the last guest leaves, you are washing glasses slowly, replaying who looked tired and whether anyone went home hungry. This is the hour you are most yourself. People meet the Cancer Rising all day: warm, receptive, quick to offer a chair. The Cancer Moon is the same creature on the inside, with a longer memory, and the Taurus Sun is the floor under both. You love by providing, and you seldom say what you would like.","Moon and Rising share Cancer, and the Moon is at home in its own sign, so what you feel and what you show are close to one animal. The Taurus Sun is a sextile to both, earth meeting water, and supplies what feeling lacks alone: a routine, a stocked pantry, a body that eats at set times. Here the Sun is the minority voice. It keeps the household running while two water lights keep the weather, and when they surge its job is to hold the floor still.","Care that arrives on time. You notice who is tired before they do, remember the birthday, the allergy and the old grief, and keep a home people want to return to. Your loyalty has no performance in it. People who have been alone for a long while sense that you will make room.","You hold on: to people, to objects, to a hurt from three winters ago. Needs go out as hints, and when the hints are missed the shell closes with a long, polite silence. Because Moon and Rising agree, nobody inside the chart argues for asking plainly. Growth is saying one direct sentence a week, such as “Sit with me tonight.”"],"taurus-cancer-leo":["You cook, tidy or refill a glass when you feel unsafe, and you do it so graciously that no one guesses the reason. The Leo Rising makes you look like the host with everything in hand. The Cancer Moon counted the chairs three days ago and is still thinking about the guest who sat alone. The Taurus Sun stands between them, keeping the pantry full and the books quiet.","Taurus and Cancer sextile, an easy and cooperative angle: the Sun builds the house and the Moon makes it a home. Leo Rising squares the Sun and sits one sign from the Moon, so the pull between standing and comfort is where the friction lives. The Sun rules your Leo Rising, and it stands in Taurus, so your public warmth is steered by a very practical planet. What looks like grandeur is often a need to be sure everyone is fed.","Generosity that remembers. You give the right thing at the right moment, you keep the birthdays, and your home, wherever it is, feels like a place where people are allowed to stop. You carry other people’s comfort as a private duty and make it look easy.","Because the giving looks so confident, nobody asks what you need, and you do not say. The Moon keeps a tally and the Sun keeps the receipts, so resentment can arrive on schedule after years of smiling. Growth is asking for one small thing aloud, before the tally gets long."],"taurus-cancer-virgo":["Three characters live in this house, and for once they have nearly the same plans. The Virgo Rising answers the door, tidy and attentive, already sorting who needs a coat. The Cancer Moon is in the kitchen, knowing what everyone ate last time and how they felt about it. The Taurus Sun keeps the lamp lit in the window and the bread in the larder. Guests feel cared for within a minute of arriving.","This chart has unusual ease: Sun and Moon sextile, Moon and Rising sextile, and the Sun trines the Rising, so the three lights form an arc in which every pair cooperates. Earth, water and earth make a quiet, nourishing mixture. Mercury rules the Rising, so care comes out as practical attention: lists, repairs, remembered preferences. With so little friction the risk is not conflict but sameness. You are very good at looking after people and may need reminding to be looked after.","Care that is actually useful. You notice what is missing from the shelf before the guest does, you remember the allergy and the anniversary, and you make a household run quietly. People feel safe around you, and the safety is built from many small accurate acts.","Everything is easy when you are the one giving, and harder when you are the one receiving, so help offered to you may be deflected with great efficiency. The Moon keeps a private ledger of what you have done, and the Sun dislikes asking. Growth is accepting a favour without repaying it that week."],"taurus-cancer-libra":["You are seen laying one more place than the guest list needs, and setting out a spare cup in case someone arrives late. The Libra Rising makes the evening graceful and fair. The Cancer Moon makes it a home, and is quietly alarmed whenever the harmony strains. The Taurus Sun carries the groceries. You remember who was hurt by what, and you seat them so it does not happen again.","Cancer Moon and Libra Rising square each other, both cardinal, so the need to nest and the wish to keep company with everyone pull at right angles: home against society, feeling against form. The Taurus Sun sextiles the Moon, an easy and cooperative angle, and backs the nesting. It stands five signs from the Rising. Venus rules Sun and Rising, so the same sweetness serves the evening and the household.","Graceful care. You make a room feel fair and a home feel safe, and you do both with taste. You are loyal to the people in your inner ring and courteous to the ones outside it, and you know the difference without making anyone feel it.","The Moon wants to protect and the Rising wants to please, so you may smooth over an injury rather than name it, and it is the Moon that remembers. The Sun then holds a quiet line against the offender. Growth is saying “that hurt me” to the person who did it, instead of to the washing-up."],"taurus-cancer-scorpio":["People read the level gaze of the Scorpio Rising and conclude you are cold, perhaps formidable. They have the wrong room. You remember how everyone takes their tea, ring on the anniversary nobody else marked and keep a spare bed made. The Cancer Moon needs a home, and the people in it fed and safe. The Taurus Sun makes that home real, with a good lock, a full pantry and a fixed address in someone’s life.","Water supports you on two sides: the Cancer Moon and the Scorpio Rising are a trine, so need and manner flow together with unusual ease. The Sun is the odd one out, an earth sign across the wheel from the Rising, and it builds the container the water is kept in. The ease has a price: with feeling and guardedness agreeing, nobody inside you suggests that a risk might be safe. Calm for you means a locked door and a lit kitchen, in that order.","Protective loyalty with practical hands. You sense what a room needs before it asks, you can be fierce on behalf of someone smaller, and you build households, businesses and friendships that outlast moods. People tell you things because your silence is trustworthy and your kitchen is warm.","Safety can become the only value, so anything unpredictable is treated as a threat and old hurts are kept dry and ready. The Moon retreats indoors, the Rising watches from the doorway and the Sun refuses to rearrange the furniture. Growth is letting one person in before they have passed every test, and counting a warm welcome as evidence."],"taurus-cancer-sagittarius":["Your favourite hour is the one just after the last guest leaves, with the plates stacked and the house exhaling around you. The Sagittarius Rising throws the evening open: laughter, news, a stranger from the station you have somehow invited. The Cancer Moon is the one who stays up to be sure everyone got home. The Taurus Sun wants the whole arrangement warm, solvent and repeatable. People think you are a sociable adventurer. Those closest know you keep the lamp.","This is a yod by sign. The Taurus Sun and Cancer Moon are a sextile, so your will and your instincts cooperate easily, and both stand at a quincunx to the Sagittarius Rising. The Rising is therefore the light that never quite fits the others, and it asks for constant adjustment: a bright public manner over a private love of home. That adjustment is the work of your life. You do it well when home is the base the adventure returns to.","Open-handed domestic warmth. You make strangers feel like family within an evening and family feel like honoured guests. You are practical, hopeful and good with food, money and memory, and others turn to you when a house needs to feel like a home.","Two lights ask for shelter and one asks for the road, so you can end up hosting everyone and resting with no one. The Moon feels what it has not said, the Rising laughs it off, and the Sun keeps cooking. Growth is telling one trusted person, plainly and early, what you need from the evening, instead of waiting for them to notice from the dishes."],"taurus-cancer-capricorn":["You show love by logistics: the lift home, the packed lunch, the form filled in before anyone asked. The Capricorn Rising keeps your manner formal, dry and a little reserved, so tenderness is rarely stated. The Cancer Moon, directly opposite, needs the opposite of formality: to be held, fed and remembered. The Sun in Taurus makes the whole project solid, with a pantry that is always full and a promise that is always kept. Those who know you well know the reserve is a coat on a very warm house.","The Cancer Moon and the Capricorn Rising face each other across the wheel, so feeling and duty sit on a seesaw: you want to be soft in private and look competent in public, and each demand can feel like a betrayal of the other. The Sun is a sextile to the Moon and a trine to the Rising, so it is friendly to both and acts as diplomat between them. The Moon is at home in its own sign, and the warmth is strong enough to thaw the manner, given time.","Practical devotion. You build homes, businesses and families that actually function, you remember what matters to each person, and you turn duty into a form of affection. In a crisis you have already made the soup and checked the insurance.","Needs go unspoken because speaking feels unbecoming. The Moon expects to be intuited and the Rising does not ask, so you may feel unappreciated by people who never knew there was an invoice. Growth is saying “I would like some looking after” once a month, in plain words, and noticing who steps forward."],"taurus-cancer-aquarius":["Three people are awake in the kitchen at midnight. The Sun is making toast. The Cancer Moon stands at the window, listening to see who is still out. The Aquarius Rising is on the phone to someone in another time zone, explaining why the toast should be made differently. Neighbours see the friendly eccentric. Family knows the one who is guarding the door. The pantry holds both.","Taurus Sun and Cancer Moon are a sextile, so the self and the need cooperate warmly: food, family, a home that holds. The Aquarius Rising squares the Sun and stands out of step with the Moon, so the manner you present, cool, original and sociable, never quite matches the tender thing it covers. The Moon is at home in its own sign and has plenty of strength. It just prefers not to be photographed.","Warmth with range. You make a family out of people nobody else would think to seat together, you remember birthdays across three continents, and you protect your own with a mixture of tenderness and unconventional ideas. People feel that you are on their side, and also on the side of the future.","The need to be held and the manner of being detached sit uneasily, so affection is offered as practical help and received as such. The Moon wants to be asked how it is. The Rising answers “fine”. Growth is telling someone the true, soft answer and hearing it said aloud."],"taurus-cancer-pisces":["You stand at an open drawer with an old photograph in each hand, turning them toward the window as though the light might say what happened. The Cancer Moon keeps everything: names, smells, the way someone laughed in 1998. The Pisces Rising, a gentle trine away, makes you look soft, receptive and a little elsewhere, so that people tell you things unprompted. Your Taurus Sun holds the whole arrangement in a cupboard that is dry, ordered and always locked against the damp.","Two water lights and an earth Sun make an arc of ease: the Taurus Sun is a sextile to both the Cancer Moon and the Pisces Rising, and Moon and Rising are a trine, so all three cooperate and nothing is truly at odds. The feeling and the face flow together, and the Sun gives the flow a bank. The risk of an easy chart is how little it argues: the water can keep rising while the cupboard stays dry, and the Sun may be the last to notice.","Tender memory with practical hands. You remember what people need and make it appear: a meal, a blanket, the right word at the right hour. You are intuitive without being flaky, and a safe harbour for people who cannot explain what is wrong.","Feeling and appearance agree so well that you can drift for years in a shared sentiment, with the Sun supplying comfort and no one supplying a plan. Nostalgia becomes a place to live. Growth is turning one memory a month into one action: a letter sent, a visit paid, a drawer emptied."],"taurus-leo-aries":["By fifty you tend to understand what at twenty you could not believe: the whole room was never the point, only the few who looked back. Until then you walk into every gathering with the Aries Rising’s bright, direct stride, and the Leo Moon quietly checks who noticed. A slight stings fast, and you cover it with a joke. Your Taurus Sun, meanwhile, is satisfied by a long friendship and a good meal, which may be more than any ovation has given you.","Your Leo Moon squares the Taurus Sun, both fixed, so you are stubborn about two different things. The Sun wants quiet worth and ordinary pleasures; the Moon wants to be seen enjoying them. You can feel unnoticed while performing well. The Moon trines the Aries Rising, both fire, so warmth leaves you with no effort and a flourish. That ease is a gift and a snare, because the room claps for the entrance and rarely reaches the person at the table.","Generous warmth with a spine. You make people feel chosen, and because the Taurus Sun stands behind it, you remember birthdays, keep promises and turn up when it is dull. You are funny, loyal, quick to cheer and slow to quit. A flat evening lifts when you are openly delighted by it.","You can need applause and call it taste, and a moment of being overlooked can set into a grudge, since two fixed lights hold on to a slight. Pride may stop you asking for what you want, so you perform instead. Growth is asking plainly to be seen by one person, and counting the friend who never clapped."],"taurus-leo-taurus":["You do not like being fussed over, and you are unhappy when nobody does. Both are true. The Taurus lights want a quiet life, a good chair and no spectacle. The Leo Moon wants warmth, colour and play, and a person who looks up and says, I see what you did there. The applause you want is specific: someone noticing the stitching, the seasoning, the three weeks it took. A crowd is nice. One attentive face at the table is better.","Sun and Moon square each other, Moon and Rising square each other, and all three lights are fixed, so nobody blinks. The Taurus pair builds in silence and expects the result to speak. The Leo Moon wants the credit spoken aloud. Leo is ruled by the Sun, so your Moon takes orders from the very light it squares, which makes the quarrel feel like family. The friction is useful: it heats the calm and disciplines the glow.","Generosity with craftsmanship behind it. You give warm, well-made things and the praise to go with them, so people feel chosen. You are loyal, dryly funny, good at celebrations that actually feel like celebrations, and able to stay calm while everyone else is panicking.","Being overlooked hurts more than the calm lets on, and two fixed lights hold a bruise until it becomes a grudge. You may over-give, over-spend or over-host in order to be thanked. Growth is asking one person for the specific praise you want, in plain words, and then accepting it without arguing the compliment down."],"taurus-leo-gemini":["Your chest lifts first. When someone says your idea was good, the breath goes high, the shoulders square and a warmth spreads behind the ribs that you cover at once with a remark. People meet a fluent, light-handed talker who seems to need nothing. The Leo Moon needs a great deal: warmth, notice, play, someone who looks at you and means it. The Taurus Sun will not ask for any of it, because asking feels like bargaining.","Taurus and Leo are both fixed and square each other, so Sun and Moon want different things stubbornly: quiet worth built over years against applause this evening. Gemini Rising sextiles the Moon, an easy angle, which hands the fire a stage and a script. That helps and it flatters. Your charm lets the Moon be seen while the Sun stays unconvinced, so you can win the room and still go home hungry.","Warmth with substance. You are generous, funny and loyal, and you finish what you promise. You can make a guest feel like the best company at the table and then follow up three months later. You show affection through small, exact acts: the gift chosen well, the song remembered, the seat saved.","Pride can go quiet and stay there. You may joke about a hurt rather than mention it, then keep a long silent grudge against people who failed to guess. The square sets comfort against the need to be seen, so you refuse the stage and resent the dark. Growth is asking, plainly and once, “I would like you to notice this.”"],"taurus-leo-cancer":["A quilt is stitched by lamplight over months, then goes on a bed where nobody comments on the work. You know that feeling. People meet the Cancer Rising: a warm, reserved presence that makes room and asks for nothing. The Leo Moon is the part that waits, quite hopefully, to be told the stitching is beautiful. The Taurus Sun just keeps sewing, content to build well, and faintly wounded that building well is not enough.","Taurus and Leo are square, both fixed, so Sun and Moon refuse to give way to each other: one builds slowly and in private, the other wants the building to be seen. The Cancer Rising stands a short step from the Moon, close but unacquainted, and its instinct is to shelter rather than shine. The Moon is the light that does not get what it asks for, so it asks louder, usually by sulking or by sudden, magnificent generosity.","Craft with warmth. You make things well and give them with real flair: the meal that feels like an occasion, the present chosen a month early, the toast that someone remembers for years. You are loyal in public and in private, and you can make a plain house feel like a place where something good is about to happen.","You may give in order to be noticed, then hide the disappointment when notice comes late. The Cancer front says “it was nothing” while the Leo Moon keeps count, and the Taurus Sun decides the debt is real. Growth is asking for a specific word of thanks, out loud, and letting the quilt be admired while you are still in the room."],"taurus-leo-leo":["Did that land, or was I only loud? You ask it quietly after most evenings, and nobody who watched you glow at the table would guess. The Leo Moon and the Leo Rising speak with one voice, so the warmth, the colour and the wish to be seen are the same from the first hello to the last. The Taurus Sun is the stubborn engine under the light, and it resents being treated as a supporting act.","Moon and Rising stand together in Leo, so what you need and how you arrive match, with no gap and no outside view. The Sun in Taurus squares them both. That square is the quarrel of this chart: the self you are building wants steadiness, value and rest, while the two lights in front of it want applause, play and a stage. All three are fixed, so nobody gives way first. You come out warm, proud and very stubborn about being thanked.","Warmth a household can be built on. You celebrate other people sincerely, remember what pleased them and put in the unseen labour that makes an evening feel generous. When you commit, the loyalty lasts, and your pride is a good reason to do things properly.","Being overlooked wounds the Moon, and the Sun answers by digging in, so a missed thank-you can become a long cold season. You may read silence as rejection and then punish it. Growth is asking for the notice you want in plain words, and letting the answer be smaller than your hope."],"taurus-leo-virgo":["Looking back from old age, you will see that the part of you that wanted to be noticed and the part that wanted to be useful were never at war, only badly introduced. For now the Virgo Rising offers modest competence and quiet help, and the Leo Moon waits in the wings for someone to say it was beautiful. The Taurus Sun is patient enough to keep working until somebody does.","The Taurus Sun squares the Leo Moon, both fixed, so what you are building and what you need to feel loved pull against each other with equal stubbornness. The Sun wants substance and steadiness. The Moon wants warmth and a turn in the light. Virgo Rising trines the Sun and sits one sign from the Moon, so the front you present is practical, helpful and a little self-effacing, and it hides the Moon’s hunger very well, even from you.","Devotion with finish. You pour care into the details of what you make and give, so the result is polished and loved. You are loyal to the people you serve, quietly warm, and generous with real praise when someone else has worked well.","The Moon wants to be noticed and the Rising pretends it does not, so a faint ache follows work that is done and nobody mentions. You may then grow fussier about the details to avoid feeling overlooked. Growth is letting yourself be seen finishing, and enjoying the applause when it comes."],"taurus-leo-libra":["You love to be looked at, and you cannot enjoy it if the person next to you is not looked at too. The Leo Moon needs warmth, notice and a good turn in the light. The Libra Rising makes that need graceful by sharing the stage with everyone, so you are charming rather than commanding, and people leave feeling included. The Taurus Sun makes sure the evening is also well catered.","The Taurus Sun squares the Leo Moon, both fixed, so the quiet self and the wish for applause pull against each other with equal stubbornness. Libra Rising sextiles the Moon, an easy angle, and gives it a gracious way to be seen. It stands five signs from the Sun. Venus rules Sun and Rising, so beauty and ease are native to both. The friction is real but pleasant, and rarely shows beyond a stubborn jaw.","Charisma with good manners. You make the shy feel visible and the bold feel welcome, and you bring a sense of occasion to small things. You are loyal, generous and truly pleased by other people’s success, which is why they are pleased by yours.","If the applause goes elsewhere the Moon is hurt and the Rising smiles anyway, so the wound is hidden behind good manners. The Sun then holds a long quiet grudge. Growth is asking for what you need in order to be seen, in plain words, and letting it be less than the whole spotlight."],"taurus-leo-scorpio":["You carry it in the chest and the jaw. The chest lifts when you are truly appreciated, the jaw sets when you are overlooked, and the face between them stays almost perfectly still. The Scorpio Rising gives you a gaze that makes people sit straighter. The Leo Moon needs to be loved out loud and will not ask. The Sun in Taurus keeps working, convinced that quality will eventually be noticed, and takes it badly when the wait is long.","This is a T-square by sign, and all three signs are fixed, so nobody gives way. Taurus Sun and Scorpio Rising face each other across the wheel, and the Leo Moon squares them both, so the need for warmth and applause sits at the point of every disagreement between what you are and how you appear. The Sun wants quiet worth, the Rising wants privacy, and the Moon wants a standing ovation it will deny wanting. Pride is the pressure valve and sometimes the leak.","Magnetism with warmth in it. You are generous in a way that is felt, loyal beyond reason, and impressive in rooms that need someone to hold the centre. You can sustain a craft, a household or a friendship for decades, and you give the people you love the sense that they are the audience that matters.","Wounded pride turns to silence and the silence turns to a verdict. You may withdraw to test whether you are missed, then hold the answer against people who never knew there was a question. Growth is asking, in plain words and in the same week, for the appreciation you were hoping would arrive unprompted."],"taurus-leo-sagittarius":["A campfire built on wet soil: twenty minutes of smoke and patience, then a roar that makes everyone lean in and start telling stories. You work on a room the same way. The Sun in Taurus lays the fire slowly and properly. The Leo Moon needs it to blaze and the people around it to be glad. The Sagittarius Rising throws on the first big log, with a joke. Strangers see sudden warmth. You know how much quiet preparation it took.","Two fire lights and an earth Sun. Leo Moon and Sagittarius Rising are a trine, so need and manner flow together with a lot of heat and generosity. The Taurus Sun squares the Moon, both fixed, so who you are becoming and what soothes you argue like old friends over who deserves the credit: the builder who wants it to last, or the host who wants it to shine. The Rising stands at a slant to the Sun, a reminder that you charm broadly and commit narrowly.","Warmth with follow-through. You are generous, funny and good at making people feel chosen, and unlike many bright people you also do the washing-up. You can lead a gathering, a family or a business with the same mix of festivity and reliability, and people leave your company a little braver.","The Moon needs to be seen and the Sun wants to be right, so a lack of appreciation can harden into a very polite refusal to help. The Rising covers it with a laugh. Growth is asking for the thanks you want, in plain words, while it can still be given freely and before the resentment sets."],"taurus-leo-capricorn":["Will anyone notice, and would it be undignified to ask? You wonder it quietly after a long job well done. The Capricorn Rising has taught you to look composed, to underplay and to let results speak. The Leo Moon needs to be applauded, to give a gift that is received with delight, and to be laughed with. Your Sun in Taurus squares that Moon, wanting the work to be good whether anyone watches or not. The three do not quite agree. The warm, proud, generous one does come through, if people wait.","Taurus Sun and Capricorn Rising are earth in trine, so what you are and how you appear agree easily: reliable, unshowy, built to last. The Leo Moon squares the Sun, both fixed, and stands sideways to the Rising, so the need for warmth, play and applause keeps colliding with a manner that treats display as slightly embarrassing. It is a difficult arrangement for a Moon that wants to be seen and a self that wants to be dignified.","Quiet generosity with real presence. You are a devoted parent, mentor and friend who gives time, money and attention freely and does the unglamorous work that makes others shine. When you do step forward, your authority is warm and utterly credible.","Pride that will not ask. Hurt is converted into stiffness, the Rising’s cool politeness takes over, and the Sun stays loyal to the grievance. Growth is claiming a little limelight on purpose, in small doses, and saying “that mattered to me” when it did."],"taurus-leo-aquarius":["By fifty you will understand that you wanted to be admired and left alone in the same breath. The Leo Moon needs warmth, play and a standing ovation. The Aquarius Rising, directly opposite, stays cool and friendly, with an air of belonging to the group and also to the future. The Sun in Taurus squares them both and takes the strain: it wants to be good, solid and quietly loved, with no fuss. People are drawn to you and cannot say whether you are a friend or a legend.","This is a T-square by sign, and all three are fixed. Leo Moon and Aquarius Rising face each other across the wheel, so the wish for personal warmth and the wish for detachment balance on a narrow beam, and the Taurus Sun squares both, standing at the corner where the pressure arrives. Nobody gives way first. The Sun wants the work to stand without applause, the Moon wants the applause, and the Rising wants to be seen as above wanting it.","Big-hearted originality. You are generous in public and loyal in private, and you can lead a group with both warmth and a refreshing lack of ego. Your personal style is memorable, your word is solid, and people feel both included and inspired.","The Moon needs to be seen and the Rising refuses to ask, so hurt is hidden behind good humour and then withdrawn into a polite distance. The Sun supports the withdrawal. Growth is saying “I would like you to notice this” once, lightly, and letting the pride go on holiday."],"taurus-leo-pisces":["You want applause, and you look as if you wandered onto the stage by accident. The Leo Moon needs warmth, play and to be seen being generous. The Pisces Rising makes you gentle, dreamy and apologetic in the doorway, so that the audience leans in to catch what you say. The Sun in Taurus squares the Moon and makes both of them wait for the thing to be done properly, since quality, it believes, will eventually be noticed.","Taurus Sun and Leo Moon square each other, both fixed, so the self and the need argue stubbornly about pride and patience: the builder wants the work left alone, the performer wants it acknowledged. The Pisces Rising is a friendly sextile to the Sun and an awkward angle to the Moon, so the gentle, receptive face is more at ease with the one than the other. It softens the Sun and veils the Moon.","Warm, sensitive charisma. You read the audience and keep it comfortable, you give generously and unfussily, and you make beautiful things with real care. People feel entertained and looked after in the same evening, and they remember who made it feel so easy.","The Rising hides the want, the Moon is hurt that it goes unseen, and the Sun waits for justice. Praise is deflected and then missed. Growth is accepting a compliment with a plain “thank you” and letting the room see you enjoy it."],"taurus-virgo-aries":["Watch you at the end of a dinner party: sleeves pushed up, plates already stacked, telling the host where the leftover lasagne should go. The help is brisk, kind and not strictly optional. People meet the Aries Rising, direct and in motion, and read confidence. The Virgo Moon is what runs the dishwasher at midnight and replays small errors from the afternoon. You soothe yourself by putting things right, and the Taurus Sun sees to it that the right thing is also well made and good to eat.","Sun and Moon share earth and trine, so what you value and what you need cooperate: craft, quality, a body at ease. The Aries Rising sits five signs from the Moon, a quincunx, and the two have never been properly introduced. Mars wants a decision now. Mercury, which rules the Moon, wants every detail confirmed first. So you decide in a second and check for a week. When the Sun leads, the checking becomes craft. When the Rising leads, it becomes fidgeting.","Competence with warmth. You start fast, finish properly and improve things as you pass: the recipe, the schedule, the loose shelf. You say the true thing in plain words and back it with a favour. People lean on you because the work is right and the help is practical, and you rarely ask for credit.","The Virgo Moon audits what the Aries Rising has already done, so the critic arrives after every decision and sometimes before it. You may rework a good thing until it is merely perfect, and take your own worry as proof of conscience. Growth is leaving one task visibly unfinished overnight and watching that nothing falls."],"taurus-virgo-taurus":["Everyone assumes you are relaxed. The pace, the chair and the unhurried voice all say so, and you let them. What they miss is the Virgo Moon running a list under the calm: the tap that drips, the email unanswered, the thing you could have done better on Tuesday. You rest the way some people tidy, with one eye open. The clean counter at ten at night is not fussiness. It is how you settle your nerves.","Sun, Moon and Rising are all earth, so the Virgo Moon shares the Taurus language of hands, food, tools and repair, and the trine between them makes this ease so natural you hardly notice it. The difference is tempo and temper. Venus likes the thing as it is. Mercury sees what it could be. The two can stand in one kitchen for an hour, one saying lovely and the other saying almost.","Quiet competence that people stop noticing because it always works. You fix, plan, cook and finish, and you do it with taste. Your care is practical: the right plaster in the right drawer, the form already filled in. Families and colleagues rest because you have already checked.","The inner critic uses the Moon’s eye for detail as a ruler held to your own knuckles, so nothing is finished enough to enjoy. You can work past hunger and tiredness and call it character, and the calm manner keeps anyone from guessing. Growth is leaving one task undone on purpose and letting the meal, the bath or the walk count as the work."],"taurus-virgo-gemini":["At three in the morning the list begins. Did you answer that email, is the milk out, was that remark in the meeting careless? By daylight none of it shows. The Gemini face is amused and ready, and the Taurus Sun is enjoying a proper breakfast. Still, the Virgo Moon carries on its quiet inspection, and it is both your anxiety and your craftsmanship. Mercury rules the Moon and the Rising, so the worry turns into questions and the questions into lists.","Taurus and Virgo are both earth and share an easy trine, so practical sense passes between them, so smoothly that you may not notice you are doing it. The friction lives between Moon and Rising. Both are mutable and Mercury-ruled, yet earth stands against air: one wants to fix things, the other wants to discuss them. That square keeps the thinking busy. The Sun is the calm one, and it prefers the finished result to the fifth revision.","Useful intelligence. You see what needs doing, explain it clearly and then do it properly, a rarer triple than it sounds. You give advice that survives contact with real life, you improve things quietly, and your care arrives as a repaired hinge, a better draft or a meal made right.","The Moon-Rising square can turn your thinking into a loop: you correct, re-correct, talk the worry round the table and call it preparation. Standards can curdle into a low hum of criticism aimed at yourself and sometimes at others. Growth is declaring one thing finished and letting the Taurus Sun enjoy it."],"taurus-virgo-cancer":["When you are tired, you reorganise the spice drawer. When you are delighted, you mend something for whoever delighted you. When you are cornered, you put the kettle on and write a list. People meet the Cancer Rising: a gentle, helpful presence who spots a loose button across a table. The Virgo Moon runs the list, a low weather of worry that tidying calms. The Taurus Sun keeps all of it unhurried, and the house smells of something good.","Taurus and Virgo are both earth, so Sun and Moon cooperate with almost no effort: one wants the good thing built, the other wants it built correctly. The Rising joins both from the water side, which makes your usefulness warm as well as exact. Everything flows, and that is the cost as well as the comfort. Nobody in the chart objects when you take on one task too many, and the Cancer front is built to say yes.","Competence you can lean on. You notice the leak, the allergy and the overdue appointment, and you fix them without making anyone feel small. Food, order and a clear head are how you love, and people in trouble end up in your kitchen because they leave it better than they arrived.","Worry can pass for love. You may run a household on your own vigilance, resent that nobody saw, and let the Virgo Moon turn the resentment into a tidier list. Help offered as a correction can land as criticism. Growth is leaving one thing unfixed on purpose and sitting down in the mess with someone."],"taurus-virgo-leo":["Three voices share one house. The Leo Rising answers the door in its best coat and says come in, sit anywhere. The Virgo Moon is already in the kitchen counting cups and noticing which one has a chip. The Taurus Sun sits in the good armchair, unbothered, certain the evening will go well because it was planned. Guests meet the first voice, are fed by the second and rest in the third.","Taurus and Virgo are both earth and trine, so Sun and Moon cooperate: what you value and what soothes you are practical, physical and slightly tidy. Leo Rising is the odd one out, a fire sign squaring the Sun and one sign from the Moon. It wants flourish where the other two want function. You are most at ease when the flourish serves the function, a beautiful and well-run thing, and most strained when it is there only for show.","Quiet excellence made presentable. You do the work properly and then dress it as a gift, so people receive both the result and the care. You notice the detail others skip, you are patient with practice, and your standards climb without turning cruel.","The Moon audits the performance while the Rising gives it, so an evening that went well is remembered as three small errors. Praise may slide off you because the critic was seated before the applause. Growth is letting a compliment finish before you correct it."],"taurus-virgo-virgo":["At the door after the guests have gone, you straighten the hall mat, square the shoes and turn the cushion back to its angle, and you do it without noticing. The Virgo Moon and Virgo Rising are one attentive voice, so what you need and how you appear are both made of care, order and quiet usefulness. The Taurus Sun gives the pair a body, a pace and a very good reason to sit down eventually.","Moon and Rising share Virgo, so there is no gap between the face and the feeling, and no outside view on either. The Taurus Sun trines them both, so it supports and agrees with them, which is comfortable and slightly dangerous: nothing contradicts the habit of improving everything. Mercury rules the doubled sign, so worry and diligence run on the same wire. At your best the care is craft. At your worst it becomes a standard nobody can meet, including you.","Thoroughness with warmth. You do things properly, remember the detail that mattered to someone, and leave every place a little better than you found it. You are the quiet engine that keeps a household, a team or a project from falling apart.","Worry is the weather here, and the Sun’s stubbornness can make it a climate. You may handle anxiety by cleaning, correcting or planning, because those feel like control. Growth is leaving one thing unfixed on purpose and noticing that the room survives."],"taurus-virgo-libra":["People assume the elegance is the whole of you and the helpfulness a style. It is neither. The Libra Rising sets a gracious tone, but the Virgo Moon is the one who notices the dripping tap, the guest’s allergy and the figures that do not add up. The Taurus Sun shares its earth with that Moon, so the care is practical, sensual and thorough. The truth is a tasteful person with a ledger kept in pencil, ready to correct it.","Taurus Sun and Virgo Moon are both earth and trine, so who you are becoming and what soothes you work together: usefulness, craft and a body at ease. Libra Rising is the outsider, five signs from the Sun and one from the Moon, so it styles and softens what the other two do plainly. Venus rules Sun and Rising, so beauty is part of the plan. The effect is quiet competence delivered with unusually good taste.","Refined reliability. You do the work properly and then present it well, so people receive both the result and the pleasure. You are fair, observant and quietly generous, and your standards raise a room without silencing it.","The Moon audits everything and the Rising does not let the audit show, so you may smile through a standard you privately think has not been met. The Sun then stands stubbornly by the correction instead of voicing it. Growth is naming the criticism in a friendly voice, early, before it becomes a verdict."],"taurus-virgo-scorpio":["At six in the morning, before anyone else is up, your desk is clear and the day’s problems are sorted into those you can fix and those you will quietly outlast. The Virgo Moon needs order and a purpose to be useful to. The Scorpio Rising adds a stillness in which no error goes unseen. The Taurus Sun makes it all pleasurable, with good tools, good coffee and craft done properly. Other people feel watched and, a little later, looked after.","Taurus Sun and Virgo Moon are both earth and in trine, so who you are becoming and what soothes you are closely aligned: usefulness, quality, a body well cared for. The Scorpio Rising stands opposite the Sun and a friendly sextile from the Moon, so it brings an investigator’s intensity to a practical pair of lights. The difficulty is the seesaw with the Rising, where what you build calmly is watched suspiciously from the doorway. You are most comfortable when the analysis serves the work rather than auditing the people doing it.","Precision with endurance. You find the fault in the plan, repair it and keep the repair from becoming a drama. You make a superb researcher, craftsperson, keeper of long projects and keeper of confidences, and you make quality look unfussy. People learn that your small, exact kindnesses are the real thing.","The inner critic is Moon and Rising together: one sees what is wrong, the other never forgets it. That can turn on you, as a private ledger of everything you have not managed, or on others, who sense an audit behind the courtesy. Growth is letting a thing be good enough in public, and saying “well done” aloud, including to yourself."],"taurus-virgo-sagittarius":["When you are tired you tidy, when you are cornered you make a list, and when you are delighted you tell everyone. The Virgo Moon is the tidying and the list: it needs order, usefulness and a day in which things were fixed. The Sagittarius Rising is the telling, bright and talkative and a little untidy in public. Your Sun in Taurus is the quiet competence between them, with its good boots and small, reliable pleasures. You look easy-going. Your calendar is colour-coded.","Taurus Sun and Virgo Moon are both earth and in trine, so what you are and what you need agree on usefulness and quality. The Sagittarius Rising squares the Moon, both mutable, so the sunny, expansive face keeps colliding with the Moon’s close attention to detail: the Rising wants to believe in the big picture, the Moon wants to check the figures. Jupiter rules the Rising and gives optimism a bigger budget than Virgo would. The Sun settles the matter by doing the work well.","Practical optimism. You will see the flaw in the plan and still believe the plan can be saved, which is a rare and useful pairing. You teach, repair and organise with good humour, and your enthusiasm makes other people less afraid of the detail.","The Moon’s worry and the Rising’s optimism can take turns in the same hour, so you may cheer others on while privately auditing yourself. The Sun carries on working to avoid choosing between them. Growth is saying the worry aloud as information, without apology, and hearing that the answer is rarely as bad as the audit."],"taurus-virgo-capricorn":["Three colleagues share the workshop. The Taurus Sun lays out the tools and likes the smell of oiled wood. The Virgo Moon checks every joint twice and sweeps up before leaving. The Capricorn Rising stands at the door with a clipboard, deciding what the shop is for. Nobody argues, because all three want the same thing: a job so well done that it is never mentioned again. Clients meet competence. Friends discover the dry jokes, and the astonishing patience of the sweeper.","This is a grand trine of earth: Sun, Moon and Rising are three earth signs, each at the ideal angle to the other two, so there is a closed circuit of ease. What you are, what you need and how you appear all point to usefulness, craft and reliability. The circuit has one flaw: there is no friction to wake it up. Nothing inside you argues for rest, risk or play. When the three lights are allowed a day with no output, the circuit turns warm instead of merely efficient.","Craft that endures. You do things properly, document them for the next person, and leave a place cleaner than you found it. Your standards are high but not cruel, and people trust your work because they can see you checked it twice and then enjoyed the result.","A grand trine can turn into a groove. Usefulness becomes the only measure, rest has to be justified, and worry takes the shape of a task list. Growth is doing one thing a week with no purpose except pleasure, and letting it be done badly."],"taurus-virgo-aquarius":["At the end of the day you are on an upturned crate, sorting the harvest into three baskets and humming, with a ledger beside you whose tidy columns are headed by questions. The Virgo Moon needs usefulness and order. The Aquarius Rising makes the order look like an experiment, friendly, original and a little detached. Your Sun in Taurus supports the Moon in trine and squares the Rising, so the practical self and the unusual face are always negotiating. People find you helpful, odd and hard to hurry.","Taurus Sun and Virgo Moon are both earth and in trine, so your aim and your appetite agree on usefulness, craft and a body well looked after. The Aquarius Rising squares the Sun and sits at an awkward angle to the Moon, so the manner you show, cool, original and sociable, has little in common with the careful, helpful, worried need behind it. The Sun is on the Moon’s side and quietly corrects the Rising’s more reckless plans.","Practical invention. You improve systems quietly, you see the flaw in the new idea and the use in the old one, and you make the unusual workable. You are kind in small, concrete ways, and colleagues remember you as the one who fixed the thing nobody else could name.","The Moon worries privately and the Rising insists that everything is under review, so concern gets disguised as detachment and nobody knows to help. The Sun keeps doing the work. Growth is saying “this is worrying me” to a friend, and not turning the answer into a project."],"taurus-virgo-pisces":["People take the soft focus of the Pisces Rising for vagueness and are astonished when you remember the dosage, the date and the exact wording of the promise. The Virgo Moon sits opposite the Rising and misses nothing: it sieves every room for what is off, broken or about to be needed. Your Sun in Taurus is on the Moon’s side, wanting usefulness, good bread and a table that is kept. The gentleness is real. The accuracy is also real, and it only shows when it is needed.","Virgo Moon and Pisces Rising face each other across the wheel, both mutable, so what you need and how you appear balance precision against surrender: the Moon wants to sort and fix, the Rising wants to forgive and dissolve. The Sun is a trine to the Moon and a sextile to the Rising, so it makes friends with both and is the practical hand that holds the two apart. Your usefulness is the bridge.","Compassionate competence. You notice what is wrong and say it kindly, you care for people with real skill, and you can sit with someone’s mess and make it manageable. The combination is the good nurse, the careful translator and the friend who actually follows up.","The Moon audits itself and the Rising absorbs everyone else’s troubles, so you end up responsible for more than you can carry and critical of yourself for dropping it. The Sun works on. Growth is deciding what is genuinely yours to fix, and letting the rest be the weather."],"taurus-libra-aries":["You hate arguments, and you start more of them than most people do. Both are true, and they come from the same wish. The Aries Rising speaks first and bluntly, then the Libra Moon winces at the sound of its own voice and spends the evening smoothing it over with a text, a snack or an apology disguised as a question about dinner. You are fair-minded to the bone and quick to say who is wrong. The Taurus Sun only wants a calm table, and will cook the peace if it has to.","Libra Moon and Aries Rising are an opposition, a seesaw between self and other: the Rising acts alone, the Moon cannot feel whole alone. Partners and friends tend to carry whichever half you have just put down. Venus rules both your Sun and your Moon, so beauty, pleasure and calm are your shared language. The Sun and Moon form a quincunx, though, so you adjust constantly: Taurus wants the same dinner, Libra wants everyone consulted first.","Courage with manners. You can say the hard thing and then make the room comfortable again, which is rarer than either half. You see both sides quickly, notice who is being left out and bring good food and good taste to the truce. People forgive you fast because you apologise fast and mean it.","The seesaw can have you attacking, then conceding, then resenting the concession. You may swing from the first sharp word to the too-quick peace without ever naming what you wanted. Growth is deciding what you need before the argument begins, and holding that position gently while the other person flinches."],"taurus-libra-taurus":["When two people at the table go quiet at the same moment, your jaw sets and your shoulders rise an inch. You stand with your weight even on both feet, as if a scale were balanced across your hips. Tension reaches your body long before it reaches your vocabulary. The Taurus calm hides this well, but the Libra Moon is always weighing: who is left out, who is overheard, what would make the evening kinder. You decide more slowly with nobody to think it through with.","Venus rules all three lights, which ties them together even though they barely recognise one another. Sun and Rising want a good meal for the body, privately enjoyed. The Libra Moon wants the same meal shared, with harmony laid on top. Taurus is fixed and earthy, Libra cardinal and airy, so you keep adjusting between one appetite and the other. The seam is where you do your best work as a host.","Peacemaking with taste. You make rooms and relationships fair and pleasant, and you do it with real physical ease. You notice who has been left out, argue both sides without losing warmth, and turn a house, a table or a negotiation into somewhere people want to stay.","The Moon will pay nearly any price for peace, and the Taurus lights will not admit it is a price. You may agree in the room and refuse later in silence, an immovability that surprises people who heard yes. Growth is saying no while it is still small, in a warm voice, and trusting the friendship to survive being weighed."],"taurus-libra-gemini":["Hang wind chimes in a pear tree and the whole garden becomes sensitive to every breeze. The pear tree is your Taurus Sun, rooted and generous. The chimes are the Libra Moon, which needs peace and company and rings at the first sour note in a room, often in the stomach before anywhere else. The breeze is the Gemini Rising, arriving with conversation and making all of it charming. Visitors enjoy the music and never notice how carefully you hung it.","Venus rules both your Sun and your Moon, so a love of pleasure, fairness and a well-laid table runs through each. Yet Taurus and Libra sit in a quincunx, which means ongoing adjustment instead of agreement between the one who stays put and the one who keeps the peace. The Libra Moon and the Gemini Rising are both air and trine, so feeling goes straight into talk. The cost of that ease is that charm can dissolve a tension before the Sun has spoken.","Graceful company. You make peace without surrendering the table, you put people at ease with a phrase, and you mediate so that both sides leave feeling clever. Your taste is sure, your manners warm, and you see what will make a gathering work before anyone has arrived.","Peace can become your first priority and your last honesty. You may agree lightly to avoid a ripple, then be surprised by a slow, stubborn refusal that surfaces from the Sun days later. Charm postpones the real conversation. Growth is saying the small unwelcome thing early, while the chimes are only humming."],"taurus-libra-cancer":["Did that land all right? You ask it after dinners, phone calls and every decision that touches someone else, in a voice that is only half joking. People meet the Cancer Rising: a soft welcome, a good host’s eye on every glass. The Libra Moon is why. You feel tension in your body before anyone names it, and you want a companion and a fair outcome. The Taurus Sun is the one who actually arranges the flowers.","Venus rules both Sun and Moon, so your taste, your warmth and your wish for peace come from one source, even though Taurus and Libra share neither element nor mode and sit at an awkward angle. Taurus wants the good thing kept, Libra wants it shared. The Moon rules your Cancer Rising and is square to it, air against water, both cardinal, so mood and welcome compete to lead and neither will wait.","Hospitality with taste. You seat the quiet guest beside the kind one, notice unfairness the moment it appears, and calm an argument by being warm and reasonable at once. People feel comfortable and respected in your company, which is rarer than it sounds.","You may keep the peace at the cost of the point. The Libra Moon weighs, the Cancer front smooths, and the Taurus Sun resents being asked to give way, so a refusal comes out late, in a single immovable sentence. Growth is naming a small disagreement in the moment, trusting that the porcelain will survive being handled."],"taurus-libra-leo":["At fifty you will understand something the thirty-year-old keeps missing: the charm was never a performance, only a way of keeping the table fair. For now the Leo Rising makes you look easy, bright and well dressed for any occasion, and the Libra Moon needs everyone in the room to be all right before you can be. The Taurus Sun, ruled like the Moon by Venus, is the part that outlasts the party.","Venus rules both Sun and Moon, so what you value and what you need share a taste for beauty, balance and company. They sit five signs apart, a quincunx, so the same taste speaks in two voices: the Sun through possessions and routine, the Moon through other people. Leo Rising sextiles the Moon and gives the courtesy a stage. It squares the Sun, so the pull between status and comfort never fully settles.","Hospitality as an art. You make a room fair without announcing it, you disagree gracefully, and you know how to arrange people and things so that everyone looks better. Your friendships last because you tend them like gardens.","Keeping the peace can turn into never choosing, and the Sun’s quiet stubbornness becomes the only vote you cast. You may agree warmly on Monday and refuse on Thursday without saying why. Growth is naming a preference early, in plain words, even if the room briefly loses its balance."],"taurus-libra-virgo":["You are strict about the details and desperate for everyone to be at ease, and you see no conflict between the two. The Virgo Rising arrives neat, attentive and a little reserved, already noticing the missing napkin. The Libra Moon needs the evening to be fair and the people in it comfortable. The Taurus Sun, ruled by the same Venus as that Moon, simply wants the table to look good and the food to be right.","Venus rules both Sun and Moon, so what you are and what you need share a taste for beauty, balance and company. They sit five signs apart, a quincunx, so the same taste speaks through different channels: the Sun through possessions and routine, the Moon through other people. Virgo Rising trines the Sun, so your manner backs your values, and it sits one sign from the Moon without quite seeing her. Mercury rules the Rising, so you reach harmony by analysis.","Refinement without snobbery. You can fix the seating plan, soften the argument and mend the loose thread before anyone knew it was there. You bring taste and service together, and people feel their comfort was thought about.","The wish for peace and the wish for correctness can prop each other up for too long, so a decision waits while you weigh a perfect answer against a kind one. The Sun then settles it by stubbornness. Growth is choosing the good-enough answer on time and trusting the relationship to carry the imperfection."],"taurus-libra-libra":["The breath goes shallow the moment a room tips out of balance, and your shoulders level themselves before you have noticed. The Libra Moon and the Libra Rising speak with one voice, so what you need and how you appear are both fairness, company and good manners. The Taurus Sun is the quiet weight at the bottom of that scale: it likes things to look right and, once it has decided, does not shift.","Moon and Rising share Libra, so the feeling and the face match, with no gap and no outside view: you are exactly as agreeable as you seem. Both stand five signs from the Taurus Sun, so the self you are building keeps being adjusted by what the pair in front of it needs. Venus rules all three signs, so the beauty and balance you value are native, but the Sun adds a stubbornness the Libra pair would rather not have.","Natural, unforced grace. You make rooms fairer, conversations kinder and tables prettier without visible effort, and you are generous with the second chance. People feel considered by you, because you really have considered them.","A pair of lights that wants peace above all can postpone every hard decision, so the Sun makes the decision eventually, abruptly and without consultation. People feel the change as a slammed door. Growth is saying what you want while there is still room to negotiate it."],"taurus-libra-scorpio":["An old oak table with a single drawer that locks: everyone is invited to the table, no one is invited to the drawer. That is your arrangement. The Libra Moon needs company, fairness and a companion at its side, and it makes you gracious and a little hard to refuse. The Scorpio Rising keeps the key on a chain and decides when to use it. The Taurus Sun, unbothered by all of it, would like a good meal, a settled home and loyalty without complications.","Venus rules both Sun and Moon here, so taste, comfort and affection come easily, but the two signs make an uneasy pair and keep adjusting to one another: Taurus wants to keep, Libra wants to weigh. The Scorpio Rising opposes the Sun and stands one sign from the Moon, which sets a guarded face over a Moon that wants harmony. You smile and assess in the same breath. Peace comes from having every conflict settled quietly in private.","Charm with a spine. You can make a hard negotiation feel like hospitality, you read people’s motives and still treat them fairly, and your word is a contract. You make loyalty look elegant and elegance reliable, which is rarer than either alone.","The Moon avoids the quarrel, the Rising records it, and the Sun declines to forgive on schedule. A pleasant surface can cover a cold ledger, and the other person learns the account only when it closes. Growth is having the awkward conversation while it is still small, and trusting that fairness survives a raised eyebrow."],"taurus-libra-sagittarius":["Who is being left out, and can I fix it before dessert? You ask it silently at every gathering. The Libra Moon needs the table to be fair and the company to be good. The Sagittarius Rising brought the guest nobody expected, laughing, with a story about the border. Your Taurus Sun lays out the food and likes that the evening is about to go well. People find you easy to talk to and hard to disappoint. You find the arrangements exhausting and delightful in about equal parts.","Venus rules both your Sun and your Moon, so beauty, comfort and companionship are native, but the two signs are an uneasy match: Taurus wants to keep what it has, Libra wants to weigh everything it might have. The Sagittarius Rising is a sextile to the Moon, so it supports the Moon’s sociability easily and adds one more light that wants more people at the table. The Sun is the one doing the adjusting. Your gift is that the adjustment looks effortless.","Hospitality with fairness. You are good at introductions, mediation and the long, warm dinner at which two rivals discover they like the same song. You are generous, curious and unusually good at making different kinds of people feel they belong in the same room.","Fairness can become a way to avoid choosing. The Moon wants everyone content, the Rising says yes to the next invitation, and the Sun stiffens quietly over the one thing you did not want to discuss. Growth is taking a side now and then, kindly, and finding that the friendships can bear it."],"taurus-libra-capricorn":["By fifty you will understand that your seriousness was never the price of admission. People had already saved you a seat, and the Libra Moon knew it all along. It needs peace, fairness and a companion, and it makes you more charming than you let on. The Capricorn Rising meets the world upright, dry-humoured and a little hard to read. Your Taurus Sun, sharing Venus with the Moon, wants good food, a good table and someone to watch the evening with from the balcony.","Venus rules both Sun and Moon, so taste, pleasure and affection are native to you, though the two signs are an uneasy fit: Taurus wants to keep, Libra wants to weigh. The Capricorn Rising trines the Sun and squares the Moon, both cardinal, so the manner you present supports the self you are building and quarrels with the need for company and ease. Duty says finish the work. The Moon asks whether the evening is fair to the people in it.","Elegant dependability. You are fair, tasteful and reliable, able to chair a meeting and then make the room feel like a party. You manage money, relationships and appearances with equal grace, and your composure helps people who are overwhelmed.","The Rising fears looking indecisive and the Moon fears conflict, so you may postpone the difficult conversation behind a well-organised calendar. The Sun then makes the call late and holds to it firmly. Growth is naming the discomfort while the issue is small, and trusting that the friendship will outlast a frank sentence."],"taurus-libra-aquarius":["You need a companion more than almost anyone, and you look as if you need nobody. The Libra Moon wants fairness, harmony and someone to share the evening with. The Aquarius Rising, in an easy trine with it, is so friendly and so detached that people assume your calendar is full. Your Taurus Sun, sharing Venus with the Moon, lays the table and hopes someone is coming. Once somebody does, the cool manner melts into very good company.","Air holds two of the lights: Libra Moon and Aquarius Rising are a trine, so what you need and how you appear flow together, sociable, fair-minded and quietly progressive. Venus rules both Sun and Moon, though the two signs make an uneasy pair: Taurus wants to keep, Libra wants to weigh. The Sun also squares the Rising, so the settled self and the modern face never quite agree about how much novelty is nice.","Fair-minded charm. You are good at making groups work: you see every side, you make the stranger feel welcome and you keep a standard of taste that is both warm and original. People confide in you because you listen without taking over.","The Moon avoids conflict, the Rising stays above it, and the Sun resents the quiet cost. Disagreements are therefore tidied away rather than settled, and a pleasant evening can hide an unmet need. Growth is saying “I would like this” before you know whether everyone will agree."],"taurus-libra-pisces":["You carry it in the inner ear: a faint tilt, as if the floor were one degree off level, and the small, constant corrections of someone trying to stand straight. The Libra Moon needs balance, fairness and a companion at the end of the day. The Pisces Rising meets the world with a soft, receptive face that agrees with everyone a little, so the horizon never quite settles. Your Taurus Sun keeps its feet on the river stone, wanting beauty, a good chair and not to be hurried through the weighing.","This is a yod by sign: Taurus Sun and Pisces Rising are a sextile, and both stand off to one side of the Libra Moon, which sits at the point of the shape. The Moon is therefore the light that must keep adjusting to the other two, and it is the one that wants fairness. Venus rules your Sun and your Moon, so sensory pleasure and harmony are native. The need is for balance, and the manner keeps tipping the scale toward whoever spoke last.","Gracious attunement. You sense what each person in a room needs and arrange for them to have it, you keep the peace without being a pushover, and you create places of real beauty and calm. People relax near you and often cannot say why.","Weighing everyone’s side, you lose track of your own. The Rising absorbs, the Moon mediates, and the Sun waits for you to sit down. Decisions are postponed until fog has settled on them. Growth is naming your own preference first, before asking what anyone else would like."],"taurus-scorpio-aries":["People assume that someone this direct has nothing to hide. You speak plainly, move fast and say what you think of the film and the boss, so they conclude they have you whole. They have not seen the cellar. The Scorpio Moon files everything: the promise, the flinch, the look that lasted a second too long. Your Taurus Sun is loyal to a fault, and when that loyalty is wounded you go quiet in a way nobody recognises, because you were never quiet before.","Mars rules your Rising and co-rules your Moon, so the chart has one temper shown two ways: a flash at the door and a slow burn below. The Moon is in its fall, which makes it earn its power through humility, and it forms a quincunx with the Rising, so the privacy and the directness hardly know each other. Sun and Moon stand opposite, Taurus across from Scorpio, a pull between trusting what is in front of you and suspecting what is behind it.","Loyalty with an iron memory. You are the one who stays at the hospital, remembers the anniversary and knows who actually helped. You tell the truth early, keep a secret for years, and protect people without display. Those who earn your trust get a defender who does not tire.","A betrayal can harden into silence before anyone notices, because your front stays friendly and fast. You may test people without telling them, then close a door on a verdict they never heard. Growth is naming the injury aloud while it still has a shape, and letting the Aries in you do what it does best: speak first."],"taurus-scorpio-taurus":["Around three in the morning, a sentence from last spring returns word for word. By day you are the pleasant, solid one with the lovely voice, and nobody guesses how closely you listen. The Scorpio Moon feels completely or not at all. It remembers who flinched and who lied gently, and the hurt does not fade. It hardens into a quiet door. Two Taurus lights stand in front of that door so convincingly that most people never learn it is there.","Two Taurus lights sit on one end of a seesaw and the Scorpio Moon alone sits at the other. Opposite signs share a modality and a theme, which here is loyalty, but they approach it from opposite sides: Taurus holds what can be touched, Scorpio what is hidden. The Moon is in its fall, so need goes underground instead of asking. You may project that intensity onto other people, and be startled when it finds a mirror.","Loyalty that is complete. You see through pleasantries to the real motive, keep a secret without strain, and stay beside someone through their worst day without flinching. You are hard to fool and impossible to bribe, and the trust you give is plain, physical and permanent.","Hurt goes down and sets, and the calm face means nobody knows a verdict has been reached. You may keep a private account of who owes you an apology, and keep adding to it. Growth is naming the injury aloud within the week, even when it feels exposing, so that forgiveness has something to work on."],"taurus-scorpio-gemini":["You answer a slight with your best joke, and then you never mention it again. People meet someone bright, talkative and easy to sit beside, and they assume nothing sticks to you. Everything sticks. The Scorpio Moon remembers the tone of voice, the date and the exact words, while the Taurus Sun, loyal to the point of obstinacy, goes on pouring tea for the person who spoke them. Trust is given slowly and withdrawn in silence.","Taurus and Scorpio face each other across the wheel, both fixed, so neither moves easily. The Sun wants ease and things to keep. The Moon wants the truth about what lies under them. That opposition tends to appear in other people, one careless and light, another secretive and intense, before you recognise both in yourself. The Scorpio Moon is in its fall, so its strength is built through humility. Gemini Rising shares no ground with it, so the chatty face cannot easily explain the dark.","Loyalty with open eyes. You notice what people leave out of a story, you keep confidences like a vault, and you are quietly relentless in a good cause. Because you are easy company, people tell you things. Because you remember, they find you are the one who actually helped.","The joke is a door that closes. You may test people silently and decide without telling them, and your forgiveness, when it comes, is an act of will rather than relief. The opposition invites you to say what happened while it is still small. Growth is naming the hurt to the person, once, in plain words, before the silence sets."],"taurus-scorpio-cancer":["Three of you live in the house, and they want different things. One sets the table, lights the lamp and would like nothing in the room moved. One goes down to the cellar to sort the old photographs and the exact words someone said years ago. One answers the door with a warm face and decides, within a minute, whether the visitor will ever get past the kitchen. Most people meet only the third.","Taurus and Scorpio face each other across the wheel, so the Sun wants to keep and the Moon wants to merge or burn: possession and total trust are two halves of one question. The Scorpio Moon is in its fall, which makes strength here something earned slowly. The trine between Moon and Rising is the quiet ally, since both are water and the front and the cellar agree about privacy. Because the Moon rules your Rising, the welcome is always shaped by what the cellar holds.","Loyalty that goes all the way down. You hold a secret without strain, notice the lie inside the pleasant remark, and make a few people feel completely safe. You stay through the long illness, the long silence and the long rebuilding, and you do not need credit for any of it.","Trust is a door you lock from the inside. The Cancer front smiles while the Scorpio Moon files the injury and the Taurus Sun refuses to reopen the case, so a small hurt can become a permanent wall. Growth is telling one person what is in the cellar before the damp sets in, and letting their answer be imperfect."],"taurus-scorpio-leo":["At the door of a crowded room you greet everyone by name, laugh at the right moment and note who arrived with whom. The Leo Rising is sincere, and so is the Scorpio Moon watching from just behind it. You give warmth freely and trust slowly. The Taurus Sun sits across the wheel from that Moon and agrees with it about one thing: what has been taken, however politely, is not forgotten.","This is a tight knot. The Taurus Sun and the Scorpio Moon are opposite, and the Leo Rising squares them both, so all three lights are fixed and pull at right angles. The Sun wants calm, pleasure and things that last. The Moon wants truth, intensity and loyalty without leaks. The Rising wants to be seen being kind. Nothing bends easily, so the energy goes into endurance, and the opposition gives you a rare ability to see the same loyalty from both sides.","Loyalty with a spine. You are generous, hard to fool and slow to wound, and once you commit to a person or a purpose you commit completely. You can keep a secret for decades and a grudge for ever, though the first is by far the more common use.","A slight can be filed behind the smile and kept for years, with the Sun’s stubbornness standing guard over it. People get tested without being told. Growth is saying “that hurt” while it is still a small sentence, before it hardens into a verdict they never saw coming."],"taurus-scorpio-virgo":["People take the neat, helpful, unassuming manner for mildness and plan around a gentle person. It is a reasonable mistake. The Virgo Rising is sincerely modest and sincerely attentive, and it notices everything, which is useful to the Scorpio Moon behind it. That Moon feels completely or not at all and remembers tone as well as words. The Taurus Sun, opposite it, will stay calm about all of this for years and then, one day, simply stop.","The Taurus Sun and the Scorpio Moon face each other across the wheel, both fixed. What you are wants calm, pleasure and a life that holds. What you need wants depth, truth and loyalty with no leaks. The Virgo Rising trines the Sun and sextiles the Moon, so it cooperates with both and acts as the go-between. Mercury rules it, so the diplomacy is practical: facts, order, a plan. It keeps the peace beautifully and the pressure quiet.","Discretion and depth. You notice what others hide, keep what you are told, and show up in practical ways when things are bad. Your loyalty has real weight, and the calm that people see is an achievement, not an absence.","The helpful front can swallow an injury politely while the Moon files it and the Sun refuses to discuss it. People who failed a test they never knew existed are confused by the sudden distance. Growth is saying the small true thing early, in a plain voice, before it needs to become a verdict."],"taurus-scorpio-libra":["At two in the morning the pleasant evening is replayed in full: who spoke warmly, who hesitated, whose compliment arrived a second late. The Libra Rising spent the night making everyone comfortable. The Scorpio Moon was keeping the real record. Opposite it, the Taurus Sun stays calm and unmoving, secure in what it owns and how it feels. You are charming by day and unforgettably thorough by night.","Taurus Sun and Scorpio Moon are opposite, both fixed, so your purpose and your comfort pull on each other like two stubborn hands on one rope: comfort and loyalty on one side, truth and intensity on the other. The Libra Rising stands five signs from the Sun and one from the Moon, so its social grace smooths the surface of a very deep arrangement. Venus rules Sun and Rising, so the beauty is real, and the Moon is the one that remembers what it cost.","Diplomacy with depth. You can bring two rivals to the same table and know exactly which of them to watch. You are a faithful friend, a calm voice in a crisis and someone whose pleasantness has real weight behind it.","The Rising keeps the surface smooth and the Moon keeps the account, so a hurt can be filed politely and held for years. The Sun then refuses to move on the matter. Growth is saying “that cost me something” while the cost is small, and letting the conversation be awkward for a few minutes."],"taurus-scorpio-scorpio":["When you are cornered you do not shout. You go still, you watch, and you begin to count. Two lights sit in Scorpio, Moon and Rising, so the feeling and the face are both intense, guarded and long-memoried. Your Sun in Taurus is the other half of the seesaw: it wants bread, warmth, a fixed address and a loyalty that never needs testing. Most days that is what you look like, until the day you are tested.","Moon and Rising share Scorpio, so the feeling and the face match with no gap and no outside view: what you feel is exactly as intense as you look. The Taurus Sun stands opposite both, and all three signs are fixed, so they lean on one another like pillars with very little give. The Moon sits in its fall here, which means safe feeling is learned through humility rather than control, and that takes time. Being seen in your tenderness is the long project the Sun keeps setting the Moon.","Depth with a work ethic. You see motive quickly, tolerate the unbearable calmly, and when you commit, the commitment is geological. People want you beside them in a crisis, because you do not flinch and you do not gossip afterwards. Your intimacy, once given, is complete.","The Moon can mistake control for safety and the Rising rewards it, so trust is demanded as proof and forgiveness is sometimes withheld as insurance. The Sun then agrees stubbornly with both. Growth is risking one honest vulnerability before you have been proven right about the person, and letting the answer arrive as it will."],"taurus-scorpio-sagittarius":["Three tenants share this house. The Sun is in the kitchen at dawn, making bread. The Scorpio Moon is down in the cellar with a lamp, keeping a very exact account of who can be trusted. The Sagittarius Rising is on the porch, waving at the street and inviting half of it in. The street thinks you are the porch. The family knows about the kitchen. Only one or two people have ever been shown the stairs.","Taurus Sun and Scorpio Moon face each other across the wheel, both fixed, so the self and the need hold each other in a long, stubborn tension: comfort and loyalty on one side, truth and intensity on the other. The Moon sits in its fall, so safe feeling is learned through humility rather than control. The Sagittarius Rising is a neighbour to the Moon, which is why a cheerful face can sit over a very serious feeling. Jupiter’s openness is the disguise, and also the medicine.","Warmth with depth. You can make a room laugh and then be the only one still listening when someone starts to cry. You are loyal, perceptive and a good friend in a crisis, and people sense that your optimism has been tested, because it has.","The Rising invites everyone in and the Moon decides privately who failed, so people may be dismissed without knowing they were on trial. The Sun stands firm on the verdict. Growth is giving an honest warning at the first small disappointment, and letting the cheerful face and the cellar occasionally agree."],"taurus-scorpio-capricorn":["At the office door you hold it open for the person behind you, nod politely, and register in one second that they are lying about something. The Capricorn Rising makes you courteous, reserved and entirely unreadable. The Scorpio Moon, directly opposite your Sun, feels everything totally or not at all, and forgets nothing. The Taurus Sun provides the calm, practical frame: a good job, a good lock, a long tenure. People think you formidable and dull. Neither is correct, but both are useful.","Taurus Sun and Capricorn Rising are earth in trine, so what you are and how you appear cooperate: composed, loyal, built to last. The Scorpio Moon opposes the Sun and sits a friendly sextile from the Rising, so the intensity of your need hides easily behind that reserve. The Moon is in its fall, which means safe feeling is learned through humility rather than control. The long project is to let a person see the feeling that the manner is guarding.","Strength with a long memory. You are effective under pressure, discreet to the point of being a vault for other people’s confidences, and capable of enormous endurance when something matters. You judge character quickly and fairly, and you are loyal to the people who pass.","Control can pass for safety. The Rising keeps the manner flawless, the Moon keeps an exact account, and the Sun refuses to admit that either needs maintenance. Resentments become a private archive. Growth is telling someone the true size of a hurt before it has aged into a case against them."],"taurus-scorpio-aquarius":["People read the friendly, slightly distant Aquarius Rising and decide that nothing sticks to you. They are wrong in a way that you encourage. The Scorpio Moon, on the far side of the wheel from your Sun, feels totally or not at all and forgets nothing: every loyalty, every slight, every scar that has become a map. The Taurus Sun keeps daily life steady, so friends see an easy, reliable, original person and rarely find the door with no handle on the outside.","This is a T-square by sign, all fixed. Taurus Sun and Scorpio Moon face each other across the wheel, and the Aquarius Rising squares both, so the pressure arrives at the point of appearance: the friendly distance is the release valve for an opposition that has nowhere else to go. The Moon sits in its fall, so safe feeling is learned through humility rather than control. The Sun wants comfort, the Moon wants truth, and the Rising wants a sky with no walls.","Loyalty with perspective. You can stay with someone through the worst year and then help them see it from above. You are discreet and unflappable, you read hidden motives without cynicism, and you keep your word after others forget what they gave.","All three lights are fixed, so changes of mind arrive as events. The Rising stays cool and the Moon stays hurt, and the Sun refuses to bring the two into one room. Growth is letting one person find the handle on the outside, and noticing that the house does not fall."],"taurus-scorpio-pisces":["At three in the morning, with rain on the roof, you are awake, turning over one sentence somebody said at dinner. The Scorpio Moon, opposite your Sun, feels totally or not at all and keeps the full record. The Pisces Rising, a trine away, is the soft, receptive face that never lets on, so nobody knows the dinner is still being examined. The Sun in Taurus wants it all to be warm again in the morning, with toast and no discussion. It usually is. The sentence is not forgotten.","Two water lights and an earth Sun. Scorpio Moon and Pisces Rising are a trine, so the feeling and the face flow together with unusual ease and very little inspection, while the Taurus Sun sits opposite the Moon and a sextile from the Rising. What you are and what you need hold a long, stubborn tension about comfort and truth. The Moon is in its fall, so safe feeling is learned through humility. The Rising makes the learning look gentle.","Deep tenderness with a long memory. You sense what is hidden and treat it with care, you keep confidences like a vault and you offer solace to those who cannot ask. In a crisis you are the soft voice that is not afraid of the dark.","Everything is felt and almost nothing is said, so hurt is filed in the water and returns, years later, as a sudden coldness. The Sun stays calm and does not explain. Growth is saying “that stung” the week it happens, in the same gentle voice you use for everyone else."],"taurus-sagittarius-aries":["Feeling arrives in your legs. When something good or bad lands, your weight tips onto your toes and you want to walk, drive or at least step outside, and usually you do. Others see the Aries Rising stride and take you for a restless sort. The Sagittarius Moon is happiest with a long road and a reason to believe in next year, and it makes jokes when it is hurt. Then the Taurus Sun calls you home, to the same chair, the same coffee and a place worth returning to.","Moon and Rising are both fire and in trine, so enthusiasm moves without friction and impulse and optimism cheer each other on. Earth stands alone here: one Taurus Sun among two fire lights. Sun and Moon sit five signs apart, in a quincunx, so the part of you that wants to stay and the part that wants the horizon keep renegotiating. Jupiter rules the Moon and Mars the Rising, and both enlarge. Venus, ruling the Sun, is the one that asks you to taste it.","Optimism that builds something. You believe in next year, and the Taurus Sun makes you the one who actually plants the thing and waits for it. You are generous with time, frank and funny, quick to forgive and glad to feed whoever turns up. People borrow your faith because it comes with a plan for lunch.","Freedom and comfort can trade places as excuses. You leave when closeness asks for patience, or stay in the warm room when the road was the point. Promises made in a good mood outrun the calendar. Growth is choosing, once, which one you are protecting, and being honest with others about the cost of the other."],"taurus-sagittarius-taurus":["A river stone is round because it has travelled, and heavy because it has stayed. You look like the stone: smooth, settled, hard to shift from the sunny spot. The shape, though, came from water. The Sagittarius Moon needs space, a long horizon and faith in tomorrow, and it goes cheerful and philosophical whenever a road appears. Your Taurus calm enjoys the road from the passenger seat with a flask of something good. Fences you build yourself are fine. Fences built by others make you restless.","Sun and Rising share Taurus, and the Moon in Sagittarius sits five signs from both, with no element or mode in common. That is the quincunx: two parts of you that have never been properly introduced. The Taurus pair wants to stay and enjoy what is here now. Jupiter’s sign wants to go and believe in what comes next. Neither is wrong, so the chart works by treaty: long trips with a known return date.","Optimism with roots. You make plans that actually leave the ground, bring guests from far away to a table already laid, and turn a place into somewhere both safe and wide. Your faith in tomorrow is contagious because you are so visibly able to pay for it today.","Comfort and freedom keep taking turns as the villain. You may bolt when a place begins to feel like a fence, then miss the bed you left, or dig in precisely because you fear what leaving would mean. Growth is booking the trip before the restlessness becomes an argument, and coming home on the day you said you would."],"taurus-sagittarius-gemini":["Can I have the open road and my own bed in the same week? You ask yourself this at airports, in bookshops and halfway through a good meal. People meet a fast talker with an opinion on everything and a curiosity about any country you name. What they do not see is how carefully you plan the return. The Sagittarius Moon wants far horizons and faith in next year. The Taurus Sun wants a door that locks and a kettle of its own.","Moon and Rising are opposed across the wheel, both mutable: Sagittarius wants the big picture and Gemini wants every small fact, a seesaw of breadth against detail. Jupiter and Mercury, the two travellers, never agree on a route. Your Taurus Sun meets the Moon in a quincunx, so wanting to stay and needing to go have never quite been introduced. The result loves travel and dreads packing, argues for freedom and renews the lease.","Appetite with roots. You bring the world home: the recipe from the trip, the language learned for a month, the friend from a long bus ride. You host travellers well and travel well for hosts. You make big ideas edible, and your optimism comes with a pantry.","You can talk about leaving for years and feel that the talking counts. Or you stay put, and feel the Moon pacing inside the walls. The opposition turns debate into a substitute for decision, and the Sun digs in at the last minute. Growth is taking one real trip and one real homecoming, and letting each be enough."],"taurus-sagittarius-cancer":["At fifty you will understand what you cannot yet at twenty-five: the itch to go was never about leaving. People meet the Cancer Rising, a warm, watchful presence who feeds travellers and keeps the porch light on. The Sagittarius Moon is the one who studies timetables at night and believes next year will be bigger. The Taurus Sun is the one who buys the sturdy bag and the return ticket. By midlife you travel as someone who is coming back.","This chart forms a yod. Sun and Rising are a sextile apart, and both stand at an awkward angle to the Moon, which becomes the point of the figure. Neither earth nor water shares anything with Sagittarius fire, so the Moon is never quite at home in the body or the house, and the other two keep adjusting around it. Because the Moon rules your Rising, the adjustments show as moods: a sudden need for air, then a sudden need for soup.","A home with an open door. You make strangers feel adopted, bring back stories and recipes from wherever you have been, and keep faith in tomorrow when others have lost it. Your optimism is practical, with a packed bag and a good meal in it, and it is catching.","The Taurus Sun resists leaving, the Sagittarius Moon resists staying, and the Cancer front takes the argument personally, so you may cancel a trip and resent the walls, or go and feel guilty on the road. Growth is planning the departure and the return as one journey, and trusting that wanting both is not a defect."],"taurus-sagittarius-leo":["You are devoted to your front door and restless to leave it, and you no longer apologise for either. The Leo Rising meets people with open-handed warmth, big laughter and a seat saved at the table. The Sagittarius Moon is already looking at the map over your guest’s shoulder. The Taurus Sun makes sure there is always bread in the house to come back to.","Fire is doubled: Leo Rising and the Sagittarius Moon trine, so the warmth you show and the freedom you need agree easily. The Sun is the odd light out. It stands five signs from the Moon, a quincunx, and squares the Rising, so your pleasures and your appetite for horizon are held together by choice rather than by nature. The house and the road both belong to you. You simply cannot be in both on the same day.","Generosity with range. You bring warmth to a table and stories from further away, and you make a rooted life feel large instead of small. People find in you a host who has been somewhere and an adventurer who remembers birthdays.","Comfort and escape can take turns winning, so you may commit with the Sun and leave in spirit with the Moon, and the people at the table feel both. Pride keeps you from admitting the restlessness. Growth is telling those you love where you go in your head, and inviting them along."],"taurus-sagittarius-virgo":["The feeling shows up in the shoulders first, a lift toward the door while your hands go on tidying the table. The Virgo Rising is attentive, practical, careful with details. The Sagittarius Moon wants space, a long road and a reason to hope about next year. The Sun is content between them, with a good meal and a known routine, glad to hear stories about places it may visit later.","The Sagittarius Moon squares the Virgo Rising, both mutable, so your need for freedom and your instinct to sort and serve pull at right angles. The Rising and the Sun are both earth and trine, so the practical half of the chart agrees with itself. The Sun sits five signs from the Moon, a quincunx, and cannot quite translate her. Mercury rules the Rising, so the mind tries to catalogue the restlessness, and the result is someone who plans adventures meticulously.","Useful wanderlust. You bring back what is worth keeping from every journey, in an order that makes it usable, and you turn a vague dream into an itinerary with the receipts already filed. Others find your curiosity warm and your reliability a relief.","The need for space may be translated into work, so a restless week looks like a new project instead of an honest wish to leave. The Moon wants a horizon and the Rising wants it scheduled. Growth is taking one unplanned afternoon and letting the Moon choose where it goes."],"taurus-sagittarius-libra":["A loaf cools on the table at dawn, and beside it a coat already hangs by the door. That is the whole household in one picture. The Libra Rising lays the table for company and talks easily with everyone. The Sagittarius Moon is the coat, wanting the next country and the next idea. The Sun is the bread: it has been baked, it is good, and it is not going anywhere.","This chart is a yod by sign. The Libra Rising and the Sagittarius Moon sextile each other, an easy and friendly angle, and both stand five signs from the Taurus Sun, which sits at the point of the shape. The Sun is the one asked to adjust, again and again, translating a social front and a restless need into a settled life. Venus rules Sun and Rising, so beauty and company are native, and the Moon supplies the horizon.","A rooted life with a wide window. You are sociable, hopeful and unusually good at making a settled place feel open. You bring home stories, flavours and friends, and you make it easy for others to believe that tomorrow can be better than today.","Because the Sun is always adjusting, you may feel a faint, unnamed restlessness inside the very comfort you built, and blame the comfort. The Rising smiles and the Moon packs a bag in the mind. Growth is choosing, on purpose, one journey a year and one routine to keep, so neither becomes an escape from the other."],"taurus-sagittarius-scorpio":["Can I trust this enough to stay, and trust it enough to leave? You ask it silently of every house, job and friend. The Scorpio Rising weighs people before it says a word. The Sagittarius Moon needs a horizon, a joke and the faith that something better is coming. The Taurus Sun wants the loaf, the lease and the loyalty. You come across as magnetic and slightly unreadable, and you are in fact a believer who has had to learn who deserves the belief.","Taurus Sun and Sagittarius Moon share neither element nor mode, so your purpose and your comfort keep adjusting to each other without ever quite agreeing. The Scorpio Rising opposes the Sun, as a seesaw, and stands a single sign from the Moon, which hides the Moon’s optimism behind a guarded gaze. People expect depth and are surprised by the laughter. The pattern settles when you let the Sun keep a home and the Moon keep a map.","A rooted life with a wide window. You are loyal and adventurous in a rare combination, you read people well enough to travel safely among them, and you bring back from every journey something useful for the household. You make hope dependable.","The Sun hoards, the Moon roams and the Rising suspects, so you can promise more than the Sun will give, or leave a room because the Rising found a reason. Restlessness may be blamed on the people nearest. Growth is deciding in advance which things you keep and which you test, and telling those who love you which is which."],"taurus-sagittarius-sagittarius":["By fifty you will understand that you were never choosing between staying and going. You were choosing what to bring with you. Moon and Rising both sit in Sagittarius, so need and manner are one cheerful, restless voice that wants horizons, stories and a reason to believe in next year. The Sun in Taurus is the quiet weight in the luggage: a good coat, a little money, a loaf for the road, a person at home to tell it all to. You look free. You are also very attached.","Moon and Rising share Sagittarius, so what you feel and how you appear match, with no gap and no outside view: you are exactly as optimistic as you seem. The Taurus Sun stands apart from both, sharing neither element nor mode, so it is the light that has to translate adventure into something you can live in. Jupiter rules the pair, which makes faith effortless and follow-through a decision. The best version of this chart is a household with a very good map on the wall.","Hope that carries weight. You encourage people sincerely and stay to see it through. You are curious, generous and free with advice that has been tested on yourself, and you can turn a wandering year into a skill, a story and a better meal.","A doubled sign gives no brake: optimism can promise things the Sun will have to pay for, and restlessness can be called freedom while it avoids a harder conversation. The Sun then goes quietly stubborn and the whole chart feels stuck. Growth is writing down the real cost of a promise before making it, and choosing one thing to see through to the end each year."],"taurus-sagittarius-capricorn":["You are an optimist with a fully stocked emergency cupboard. The Sagittarius Moon believes in next year, in the stranger’s story and in the road that opens when you stop checking the map. The Capricorn Rising meets the world with a straight back and a list. The Sun in Taurus, comfortable with the Rising, keeps the cupboard stocked and the schedule modest. People see the reliability first and meet the hope later, usually when you laugh at something that surprised you.","Taurus Sun and Capricorn Rising are earth in trine, so what you are and how you appear agree: practical, sturdy, quietly ambitious. The Sagittarius Moon is the outsider: it stands at an awkward angle to the Sun and one sign from the Rising, so the need for freedom, faith and distance keeps arriving in a chart that prefers plans. Jupiter and Saturn are an old pair, expansion and limit, and you hold both. When they agree, you get a slow, well-funded adventure.","Faith with a foundation. You encourage others and then help them budget for it. You can take a large vision and divide it into steps, hold on to your optimism through a long climb, and keep your sense of humour on the days when the road is mostly gravel.","The Moon wants to leap and the Rising wants a guarantee, so the leap is postponed until conditions are perfect, and the conditions are never perfect. The Sun stays comfortable. Growth is choosing one modest risk a year and taking it before the plan has finished arguing with the hope."],"taurus-sagittarius-aquarius":["Your weight shifts from foot to foot at a long dinner. Your eyes go to the door, then the window, then back to the person speaking, and you stay. The Sagittarius Moon needs a horizon, a library of the world and the faith that something good is next. The Aquarius Rising, a friendly sextile away, adds cheerful originality and distance. The Sun in Taurus is the one who stays and listens, because it likes this table and wants it to survive. Others see a free thinker. Loyalty is what they should be watching.","Sagittarius Moon and Aquarius Rising are a sextile, so the need for freedom and the face of originality cooperate warmly, and together they are all curiosity, ideas and open windows. The Taurus Sun squares the Rising and sits sideways to the Moon, so the self that wants one good table is always being invited to a larger one. The chart is friendly to everyone except the Sun, which gets to be the diplomat, the host and the brake.","A wide mind with a warm table. You bring ideas from many cultures and fields and make them useful at home. You are encouraging, outspoken and unusually reliable for someone so curious, and your friendships cross borders, ages and professions without visible effort.","Two lights lean away from the centre, so you can promise more than the Sun can host, or explain a departure so well that the other person never notices it was one. Growth is saying “I need to go” and “I will be back” as two separate sentences, and keeping the second."],"taurus-sagittarius-pisces":["A caravan fords a river at dusk: wheels in water, animals wading, the driver singing to keep everyone calm. That is the way you cross things. The Sagittarius Moon is the caravan, hopeful and loud and sure that the far bank has better weather. The Pisces Rising is the river, soft, wide and a little confusing in the failing light. Your Sun in Taurus is the wet soil on both banks, wanting a place to put its boots down and a hot meal when you arrive.","Jupiter rules both Moon and Rising in the older scheme, so faith and feeling speak one generous dialect. Yet the two make a square, both mutable, so the hopeful traveller and the dreamy face keep crossing paths: the Moon wants a destination, the Rising wants to drift. The Taurus Sun is a sextile to the Rising and sideways to the Moon, so it must work to follow the plan. It is the practical one that brings the tent.","Faith that feeds people. You are generous, imaginative and hard to discourage, and you make hope concrete: a meal, a map, an invitation. Others find that near you tomorrow seems more likely, and today feels less lonely.","Optimism and softness agree to avoid a hard no. You may say yes to a journey, a person or a promise and then discover the Sun cannot afford it. Disappointment lands on others as vagueness. Growth is learning to say “not this time” kindly, and letting that be an act of care."],"taurus-capricorn-aries":["At five in the morning, before anyone else is awake, you sit at the table with a list. Nothing about it is anxious. It has margins. By day people meet the Aries Rising: direct, brisk, someone who takes charge in the first minute. What they miss is the Capricorn Moon’s private scorecard of who is provided for, what is owed and what the winter will cost. You show love by arranging it, and you would sooner mend a roof than describe a feeling.","Sun and Moon trine in earth, so purpose and need cooperate: build, save, make it last. The Moon is in detriment in Capricorn, which means it works against the grain and learns feeling through tasks rather than flow. It also squares your Aries Rising: both are cardinal and both want to begin, but the Rising wants to leap and the Moon wants a foundation first. Mars rules the chart and Saturn the Moon, so you start at speed and then discover you must survive the thing for years.","Reliability with nerve. You take the hard first step, and the Moon makes sure there is a structure behind it. Your word is as good as money, your help arrives before the request, and you plan for other people’s bad weather without mentioning it. People relax when you are in charge, and mostly they are right to.","You can mistake provision for intimacy and handle a feeling like a task due on Friday. Fatigue shows as brusqueness and a clipped goodbye. You may wait to be asked for help you never admit needing. Growth is saying what you need before it has been earned, and letting someone repay a kindness slowly."],"taurus-capricorn-taurus":["When something hurts, you get more useful. You answer a feeling by doing a job: the tax return filed, the shed sorted, the lift offered to someone who had not asked. When you are tired you make a list, and when you are delighted you quietly buy the good bread. The Taurus calm makes all of this look easy. The Capricorn Moon feels privately and manages the feeling like a task, so love arrives as provision, never as speeches.","Sun, Moon and Rising are all earth, and the Moon’s trine to both Taurus lights makes your inner and outer lives agree on method: build, store, endure. The Moon sits in Capricorn, its detriment, the sign least suited to simply being soothed, so comfort is something you learn to accept rather than earn. Saturn rules the Moon, Venus the rest: a pleasure-loving person who audits their own pleasures. With no friction, the habit goes unquestioned, because nobody inside says maybe rest.","Dependable provision. You turn up, pay the bill, repair the roof and remember the appointment for three people. Your care takes the shape of structure that others can live inside, and your competence earns respect without asking for it. Over a long span you build things that outlive the weather.","You may treat rest as a reward that is always one more task away, and manage a feeling as though it were a deadline. Others often cannot tell you are struggling, because it arrives as a more efficient week. Growth is accepting one kindness without repaying it at once, and letting care be a plain pleasure."],"taurus-capricorn-gemini":["Three people share your house. The Gemini one answers the door, chats with the guests and finds the joke. The Capricorn one sits in the back room with the accounts and a faint frown, working out what everything costs. The Taurus one stands in the kitchen, wanting everyone to put down their tasks and sit. All three love you. At dinner they take turns to speak, and the table takes the best of each.","Taurus and Capricorn are both earth, so Sun and Moon share a trine: the kitchen and the ledger agree on loyalty, honest work and a dislike of waste. The Gemini Rising is the odd one out, a quincunx to the Moon and a semi-sextile to the Sun, with no shared ground with either. Mercury, the chart ruler, means that talk is the one tool all three can use. The Capricorn Moon is in detriment, so ease about feeling is learned by practice.","Competence that is good company. You can run a household, a budget or a project and keep everyone laughing while you do it. You turn promises into schedules, and your affection arrives in practical form: the booked table, the mended gutter, the thing remembered. People trust your ease because there is structure behind it.","You can mistake providing for being close, and run the chatty surface as a way of keeping real feeling out of the meeting. The ledger lengthens and the kitchen cools. Growth is letting one need onto the agenda in your own voice, and sitting down at the table before the work is done."],"taurus-capricorn-cancer":["Ten at night, and you are at the stove stirring something nobody requested, tomorrow’s lunches already lined up on the counter. People meet the Cancer Rising: a gentle, receptive manner that invites confidences. They do not see the Capricorn Moon at work behind it, managing feeling like a rota. You feel privately, handle it competently, and say “I love you” by being the one who remembers the car insurance. The Taurus Sun makes sure there is good bread.","Moon and Rising sit opposite each other, Capricorn across from Cancer, so the soft front and the sober need face off like two sides of one household: the one who nurtures and the one who runs it. The Moon is in detriment here and learns its feelings the slow way, as a skill. The Taurus Sun shares earth with the Moon and tips the balance toward the practical, so the Rising’s softness comes out only once the work is done.","Dependability that feels like love. You build savings, routines and habits that carry a family through lean years, and you do it without drama. People find in you someone who has already thought of the thing they were about to worry about. Your care is practical enough to be believed.","You may withhold the soft word and give the useful one, then feel unseen when nobody reads the invoice as affection. The Capricorn Moon files feeling under duty, and the Cancer front is too gracious to complain. Growth is saying out loud, once a week, what the provision means, and letting someone take care of you without keeping score."],"taurus-capricorn-leo":["People assume someone this warm must be careless with money, time and promises, and they are wrong in a way that costs them a little at the end of every evening. The Leo Rising sets the tone: generous, theatrical, kind. Behind it the Capricorn Moon keeps accounts, and the Taurus Sun has already put something by for winter. The truth is a showman with a ledger, moved by whatever is being built.","Taurus and Capricorn are both earth and trine, so Sun and Moon work together: what you value and what you need in order to feel safe are the same practical things, a solid income, a reliable room, work that outlasts you. Leo Rising squares the Sun and sits a quincunx from the Moon, so neither understands it. It wants to be seen and thanked. They want to build quietly. The truce is that you do the building and let the Rising take the bow.","Competence you can enjoy. You make plans that hold, keep your word with unshowy care and bring dignity to ordinary occasions. People rely on you in a crisis because the warmth and the discipline arrive in the same person.","Feelings are managed like tasks, and the Rising’s smile can persuade you that managing is the same as feeling. You may measure love by what is provided and wonder why it is never enough. Growth is letting someone do something for you that you could have done faster yourself."],"taurus-capricorn-virgo":["At six in the morning, before anyone else is up, the shape of the day is already in your head and the kettle is on. The Virgo Rising has sorted the tasks, the Capricorn Moon has ranked them, and the Taurus Sun has decided where the first proper rest will be. All three are earth and hold one grand triangle, so you give the impression of someone who has never needed to raise their voice to get things built.","This is a grand trine by sign, all of it earth: Sun, Moon and Rising each trine the other two. It is rare ease and rare completeness. What you are, what you need and how you appear all value usefulness, patience and things that last. Mercury rules the Rising, so the thinking is practical and orderly. The strain, such as it is, comes from agreement: no friction wakes you, so change has to be chosen rather than forced.","Foundations. You build the thing others stand on, reliably and without applause, and you do it in a way that improves with age. People trust the combination of patience, competence and plain speech, and they bring you the jobs that cannot go wrong.","Because the three lights agree, you can mistake your own preferences for the way the world is. Feelings are managed like tasks and tenderness arrives as provision, so people feel looked after and not quite known. Growth is asking one person a question you do not know the answer to, and listening to the end."],"taurus-capricorn-libra":["You schedule your kindness, and you are kinder for it. The Libra Rising is gracious and easy to talk to, the sort of person a whole office confides in. The Capricorn Moon is the reason there is a plan, a budget and a reliable pair of boots. The Taurus Sun shares earth with that Moon and carries the weight without comment. People feel warmly treated and quietly supported, and they rarely see the planning behind it.","Taurus Sun and Capricorn Moon are both earth and trine, so what you are and what you need agree: structure, patience, things built to last. The Libra Rising squares the Moon, both cardinal, so the pull between sociable ease and private duty is where the friction lives. It stands five signs from the Sun. Venus rules Sun and Rising, so beauty and company soften the climb. You are best when the work and the people are allowed to meet.","Dependable charm. You keep your word, you remember the occasion, and you make a long effort feel civilised. People rely on you for the unglamorous things and enjoy you for the glamorous ones, and you manage both without showing the strain.","Feelings are handled as tasks and then presented well, so the real one can stay undelivered. The Rising smiles through a bad week and the Moon makes a schedule. Growth is letting somebody see the unscheduled, ungracious version of you, once, and finding that the friendship survives it."],"taurus-capricorn-scorpio":["Three people share this house. The Taurus Sun is in the kitchen, making something that will keep. The Capricorn Moon is in the study with the accounts, convinced that tenderness is a task for later. The Scorpio Rising stands at the front window and has already decided who is allowed in. Visitors meet the one at the window. Family meets the one at the stove, and the study door stays shut until somebody is genuinely ill.","Taurus Sun and Capricorn Moon are both earth and in trine, so what you are and what you need agree on one point: build slowly, build well and do not show the scaffolding. The Scorpio Rising is a sextile to the Moon, so its guardedness helps the Moon’s reserve, which sits in detriment here and has to learn tenderness by practice. It opposes the Sun, so what you present is more intense than what you assemble. The three lights cooperate in everything but admitting need.","Endurance with a plan. You can climb a long ascent without announcing it, repair what others abandon, and take on responsibilities that would flatten a lighter temperament. Your word, your accounts and your friendships are all kept in order, and people feel the floor under them when you are near.","Needs get managed rather than felt. The Moon turns tenderness into a task, the Rising treats asking as exposure, and the Sun carries on working as though rest must be earned. The cost is a life that looks solid and feels cold at the centre. Growth is letting someone carry something for you, and thanking them without an invoice."],"taurus-capricorn-sagittarius":["At a table covered with maps, receipts and a half-eaten pear, you are working out how to see the world and still keep the house. The Sagittarius Rising is the maps: bright, curious, ready to go anywhere with the right company. The Capricorn Moon is the receipts, feeling safest when responsibilities are met and rarely admitting to being tired. Your Sun in Taurus is the pear, slowly enjoyed. Others see a cheerful, capable traveller. You see a ledger with some very good chapters in it.","Taurus Sun and Capricorn Moon are both earth and in trine, so your aim and your appetite agree: build well, save carefully, finish what you start. The Sagittarius Rising stands one sign from the Moon, an awkward neighbour, so the optimism you show and the duty you feel keep trading places. The Moon sits in detriment here, so feeling is managed like a job and has to be learned as a skill. The Sun keeps asking whether the plan is also a pleasure.","Wide vision with practical hands. You can imagine a journey and also sort the tickets, the visas and the money, and then enjoy the trip. You are good at the long game, at teaching others, and at being both the mentor and the one who actually shows up on Monday.","The Moon expects hardship and the Rising insists on cheer, so you may encourage everyone while privately carrying too much. The Sun works on. The strain appears as a sudden need to leave or to quit. Growth is saying “this is heavy” while it can still be shared, and treating rest as part of the plan rather than a reward at the end of it."],"taurus-capricorn-capricorn":["People assume you are cold, because you are punctual, composed and dry. They mistake the order for an absence of feeling. In fact Moon and Rising both sit in Capricorn, so you feel privately and manage it like a task: a list for your own tenderness, filed under later. Your Sun in Taurus is in trine with both, and wants good food, comfort and a long season of work well done. You are steadier than most people ever see and softer than almost anyone is allowed to know.","Moon and Rising share Capricorn, so what you feel and how you appear match, with no gap and no outside view: you are exactly as composed as you look. The Moon sits in detriment here, working against the grain, so tenderness has to be learned and rehearsed. The Taurus Sun is in trine with both, so the self you are building supports the manner without effort. Saturn rules the pair, which gives you patience, honour and an unforgiving ledger.","Authority that is earned. You are exceptionally dependable, capable of long preparation and cool in an emergency. You protect the people in your care without making a speech, and you are quietly funny in a way that only the attentive notice.","A doubled Saturn can become a very effective prison. Feelings are supervised, rest is rationed and affection takes the form of problem-solving. The Sun is content with the arrangement. Growth is letting one person see the unsupervised version of you, and noticing that the foundation holds."],"taurus-capricorn-aquarius":["At five in the morning, before the house stirs, you are at the desk with the stove just lit and a strange idea half drafted, its budget already in the margin. The Capricorn Moon feels privately and manages feeling like a task. The Aquarius Rising, a neighbour, makes your manner cool, friendly and a step ahead. Your Sun in Taurus is in trine with the Moon, so all of you wants things built well and built to last, even the odd things. People see an inventive, level-headed person. They rarely see how early you start.","Saturn rules both Moon and Rising in the older scheme, so duty and detachment speak one formal language, and the two signs sit one apart as neighbours with little in common. Taurus Sun and Capricorn Moon are both earth and in trine, so what you are and what you need agree: build slowly, build to last. The Moon is in detriment here, so tenderness is learned rather than assumed. The Sun squares the Rising, which means the new idea must also be comfortable.","Inventive reliability. You can turn a strange idea into a working schedule, a budget and a finished object. You are patient with long projects, honest in your assessments and quietly loyal, and people give you their most ambitious plans because they trust you to make them real.","Feeling is managed like a project and distance is called efficiency. The Moon rations tenderness, the Rising explains the rationing so reasonably that no one objects, and the Sun enjoys the order. Growth is leaving a gap in the schedule for someone who needs you with no agenda."],"taurus-capricorn-pisces":["You manage your feelings by building something with them: a shed, a budget, a garden path, a long letter you will not send. The Capricorn Moon feels privately and treats feeling as a task, which suits it badly and which it does well anyway. The Pisces Rising is the soft, absorbent face that makes people trust you before you have said a word. Your Taurus Sun is the ledger of years in which both are written down, calmly, in a good hand.","This is an arc of ease: the Taurus Sun is a trine to the Capricorn Moon and a sextile to the Pisces Rising, and Moon and Rising are also sextile, so the three lights work together in a friendly line. The Moon is in detriment, working against the grain, so tenderness has to be learned, and the Rising, a gentle water, helps it learn. Saturn gives the water banks and the water softens Saturn.","Quiet, durable compassion. You build structures that shelter vulnerable things: a business, a household, a regular Sunday. You are honest about what you can and cannot do, you keep your word, and your gentleness is made trustworthy by your reliability.","Feeling is turned into work, and the water is kept behind a wall of tasks. The Rising absorbs other people’s moods and the Moon files them, so you are tired in a way that rest alone does not touch. Growth is letting a feeling be unproductive, with nothing built from it, for one whole evening."],"taurus-aquarius-aries":["Picture a radio mast standing in the middle of an apple orchard: rooted, fruiting and in contact with something far away. That is how you look from the road. The Aries Rising is the one who walks up to say hello, direct and curious. The Aquarius Moon waits at the gate, friendly and a little distant, feeling through ideas and needing a window left open. Close friends know you as loyal company who also vanishes for an afternoon. You love your people, and you need a room of your own.","Your Taurus Sun and Aquarius Moon square each other, and both are fixed, so two kinds of stubbornness collide: one wants the familiar table, the other wants freedom and an odd opinion. Each is sure it is only being sensible. The Moon sextiles your Aries Rising, so friendly talk and fast action cooperate. You can float a strange plan and start it by teatime. Venus rules the Sun and asks you to enjoy the result; Mars rules the front and wants it done.","Independence with warmth. You are loyal without clinging, original without making a show of it, and you give friends room to be themselves. You can start something nobody has tried and then see it through to harvest. You hold your ground when the crowd is wrong, and your good humour makes dissent feel safe.","Two fixed lights can make you right and alone, attached to a plan or an opinion beyond its use. Distance can pass for calm, and closeness can be answered with a clever idea instead of a hello. Growth is staying one minute longer inside the feeling, and changing your mind when the evidence is a friend’s face."],"taurus-aquarius-taurus":["Can I be close to you and still keep one window open? You ask it silently at the kitchen table while someone you love reaches for your hand. People meet the Taurus warmth, the physical ease, the settled address, and they assume a traditional person. Then you mention the friend who builds radios, or the opinion nobody else holds. The Aquarius Moon feels through ideas and distance, and gives the odd and the unplaced a good chair. You are more at ease at a table of misfits than a table of relatives.","Sun and Moon square each other, Moon and Rising square each other, and all three lights are fixed, so nothing here bends first. The Taurus pair wants one place, one chair and familiar hands. The Aquarius Moon wants equals, room to be strange and the freedom to leave a room mid-sentence. Each sets the other’s boundary, so you feel loyal and faintly caged, rooted and faintly foreign. The usual settlement is a long attachment with a great deal of private room.","Loyalty with elbow room. You keep friends for decades and let them be strange, hold unconventional ideas with old-fashioned good manners, and carry an eccentric plan to completion because you actually finish things. People learn they can be odd in your company without losing your regard.","Distance can pass for peace: you go quiet and call it independence while someone waits at the table for a sign of you. Two fixed lights can make a retreat last longer than you meant. Growth is saying in plain words that you need space and when you will be back, so your solitude stops feeling like a verdict."],"taurus-aquarius-gemini":["What fifty knows and twenty does not: wanting to be close and wanting to be free were never an argument you had to win. For years you swung between the two, warm and talkative with friends, then abruptly a day behind a closed door. People took the swings for moods. The Taurus Sun needs home, habit and loyalty. The Aquarius Moon needs air and a free hand. The Gemini face made both look easy, and in time you learn to schedule the door.","Taurus and Aquarius are both fixed and square each other, friction between two stubborn parties: the Sun wants possession and comfort, the Moon wants autonomy and strangeness. Neither gives way first. Gemini Rising trines the Moon, both air, so ideas and feelings get along and talk becomes the escape valve. That ease is useful and slightly slippery. You can discuss the friction magnificently without changing a thing.","Loyalty without clinging. You can be a friend for forty years without demanding a reckoning, give people room, and still turn up for the move and the funeral. Your ideas are odd and your table is warm, a combination that makes outsiders comfortable. You are present and unpossessive.","You may withdraw before anyone has done anything and call it independence, or hold on to a habit and call it principle. The square is a real argument, and talk can postpone it indefinitely. Growth is telling the people close to you the schedule of your own weather, so distance reads as rest rather than rejection."],"taurus-aquarius-cancer":["You will drop everything to help a friend, and you need some evenings when nobody is invited. Both are true, and the resolution is a house with a porch: warm at the front, fenced behind. People meet the Cancer Rising: a welcoming face, soup on the stove, a habit of asking after your family. The Aquarius Moon is the one who walks out to the garden to think about something large and strange. The Taurus Sun owns the garden and will not be hurried out of it.","Sun and Moon are square, both fixed, so the builder and the free thinker are equally stubborn and neither gives way. Taurus wants to keep what it has made, Aquarius wants room to be strange, and there is no compromise to be had, only a household arranged with space for both. The Cancer Rising shares no element or mode with the Moon, so welcome and detachment seldom agree, and friends feel warmth and then a sudden absence.","Hospitality without ownership. You welcome odd people, keep friendships for decades at whatever distance suits them, and give the people you love freedom along with the soup. You see others as individuals and as a community at once, which makes you fair and kind in the same sentence.","The pattern is closeness, then withdrawal. The Cancer front draws people in, the Aquarius Moon needs air, and the Taurus Sun holds the line on both, so someone who took the welcome literally may feel dropped. You can explain it all rationally and still leave a hurt unfelt. Growth is announcing the retreat before you go: “I will be back Thursday.”"],"taurus-aquarius-leo":["The jaw sets and the smile stays where it is. That is the posture of someone who wants a close circle and an open door at the same time and gets irritated by whoever asks which. The Leo Rising pulls people in. The Aquarius Moon, directly opposite it, needs air and a friend who lets it be strange. The Taurus Sun, square to both, would like a quiet life and a good chair.","This is a T-square of fixed signs. The Aquarius Moon and the Leo Rising face each other and the Taurus Sun squares them both, so every light pulls at a right angle to another. The Rising wants warmth, the centre of the room and personal loyalty. The Moon wants distance, ideas and the freedom to be unclassifiable. The Sun wants comfort, constancy and to be left to build. Nothing yields, so the strain is carried like a muscle: strong, and sometimes sore.","Magnetism with independence. You draw people in and then treat them as equals, which they find rare. Your loyalty is real and unsentimental, you are good in a crisis because feeling does not flood the thinking, and you keep friends who are all quite different from one another.","You can leave the room emotionally while remaining in it beautifully, and others take the charm for closeness. The Sun then digs in on a principle that is really a need for space. Growth is saying “I need an hour” aloud, instead of disappearing behind good manners."],"taurus-aquarius-virgo":["An open window in a storm, and someone beside it with a cloth, wiping the sill as the rain blows in and saying it is good to have the air. That is you with the Aquarius Moon: you want the weather to come in. The Virgo Rising goes on wiping, tidy, helpful and slightly apologetic. The Taurus Sun stands behind both and would like to know who is going to pay for the curtains.","The Taurus Sun squares the Aquarius Moon, both fixed, so what you are building and what you need in order to feel free are stubborn opposites: one wants constancy, the other wants room to be unusual. Virgo Rising and Sun are earth and trine, so your manner is dependable and backs the Sun’s values, while it sits a quincunx from the Moon and cannot quite place her. Mercury rules the Rising, so you explain the Moon’s odd ideas in sensible vocabulary.","Reliable originality. You come up with the unusual solution and then make it work in practice, with the paperwork done. Friends find you generous with attention and unafraid of strangeness, and your steady manner makes other people feel safe enough to be odd.","The Rising’s helpfulness can keep people at a courteous arm’s length, so you serve everyone and are known by few. The Moon wants freedom from being managed, and the Sun manages the schedule anyway. Growth is letting one friend see the unedited version, the part that does not tidy up."],"taurus-aquarius-libra":["Can I be close to you and still be strange? You ask it silently, often over dinner, with a gracious smile and an excellent memory for everyone’s birthday. The Libra Rising wins people over in minutes. The Aquarius Moon, trine to it, enjoys them but needs a balcony and an hour alone. The Taurus Sun squares that Moon and would like to know why anyone needs distance when the soup is hot.","Libra Rising and Aquarius Moon are both air and trine, so the face you wear and the mind you need agree: sociable, fair-minded, a little detached. The Taurus Sun squares the Moon, both fixed, so the self that wants closeness, comfort and routine disagrees stubbornly with the need for freedom. It stands five signs from the Rising. Venus rules Sun and Rising, so warmth and taste are never in doubt. What is in doubt is how close is close enough.","Friendliness with originality. You are easy to talk to and impossible to predict, and you can bring a fresh angle without making anyone feel foolish. People feel included by you and also a little stimulated, which is a rare and useful combination.","Distance can masquerade as courtesy, so you may withdraw politely rather than say you need room. The Sun then insists that nothing is wrong, in a voice that closes the subject. Growth is saying “I love this and I need a night to myself” in one sentence, to the person it concerns."],"taurus-aquarius-scorpio":["By fifty you understand that you never wanted less closeness, only more room inside it. The Aquarius Moon needs air, ideas and permission to be odd. The Scorpio Rising watches from behind a calm face and lets people in by degrees. Your Taurus Sun wants a settled house and a settled heart, and cannot see why anyone would trade either for a theory. Three fixed temperaments, and none of them will blink first.","This is a T-square by sign: Taurus Sun and Scorpio Rising face each other, and the Aquarius Moon squares both, so the need for freedom and distance cuts across every arrangement between what you are and how you appear. All three are fixed, so the friction is slow and stubborn, and everything that happens is long remembered. The Sun builds, the Rising guards, and the Moon keeps opening a window in the room both of them are trying to seal.","Loyal independence. You can be counted on completely and still belong to nobody. You see what is wrong with a system before others notice it, you build slowly toward an unusual idea, and you offer friends the rare combination of faithfulness and real respect for their freedom.","Three fixed lights make for beautiful consistency and poor flexibility. Positions harden, and a disagreement can become a long silence in which each side waits to be understood first. The Moon retreats to its distance and the Rising reads the retreat as rejection. Growth is saying “I need room” early, kindly and before it sounds like a verdict on the person in front of you."],"taurus-aquarius-sagittarius":["You want to belong completely and answer to nobody, and you see no contradiction in it. The Aquarius Moon needs friends, ideas and the freedom to be odd. The Sagittarius Rising, a friendly sextile away, is cheerful and global, with opinions about the future and a friend in every time zone. Your Taurus Sun squares the Moon and would like a fixed address, a good bed and a loyal few. The resolution is a house with a very wide guest list and a very firm door.","Taurus Sun and Aquarius Moon square each other, both fixed, so your will and your instincts argue stubbornly: roots against freedom, the known against the strange. The Sagittarius Rising makes an easy angle to the Moon, so you look at ease with your own originality even while the Sun is quietly planting its heels. Three different elements give you range and a slight difficulty explaining yourself. The friction is useful when the Sun hosts and the Moon visits.","Friendly originality. You bring unusual ideas to ordinary tables and make them sound inviting. You are loyal in friendship, generous with attention and gifted at holding a long project and a brand-new idea in the same hand, which makes you valuable to any group trying to change something without wrecking it.","The Sun resists change and the Moon demands it, and the Rising explains the stalemate so charmingly that nobody notices it is one. Some decisions are therefore postponed behind a good conversation. Growth is naming which part of you wants out of the pattern and which part wants in, and letting the answer rearrange the week."],"taurus-aquarius-capricorn":["You carry it in the shoulders and the handshake, which is firm, brief and meant. The Capricorn Rising sets your manner: upright, dry and reliable, a person who is on time and expects the same. The Aquarius Moon, a neighbour in the same Saturn household, needs friends, ideas and enough room to think strange thoughts. Your Taurus Sun squares the Moon and prefers its comforts consistent. People see the officer. A few see the inventor trying to get out of the break room.","Saturn rules both Moon and Rising in the older scheme, so duty and detachment speak the same formal language, though the two signs sit one apart as awkward neighbours. The Taurus Sun squares the Aquarius Moon, both fixed, so what you are and what you need argue stubbornly about comfort and freedom: the self wants a fixed table, the need wants a window and a different conversation. The Sun trines the Rising, so your outer manner always supports the building, and the Moon has to find its own way to be strange.","Disciplined originality. You can propose a radical idea and then present the budget, the timeline and the risks. You are loyal, honest and quietly progressive, and in a group you turn a good intention into a working system.","The need for freedom gets filed under efficiency. You may keep your distance and call it professionalism, or cling to routine and call it principle. Sun and Rising agree with each other and outvote the Moon. Growth is letting a friend see the odd, unfinished idea before it has a plan, and letting the plan come second."],"taurus-aquarius-aquarius":["A signal tower stands at the end of a well-worn cattle path: the antenna is thoroughly modern and the footing is thoroughly old. That is you. Moon and Rising both sit in Aquarius, so what you feel and how you appear are the same cheerful, cool, unusual voice, interested in everyone and attached to few. The Taurus Sun squares both and keeps the tower anchored: a love of food, loyalty and a habitual route. People hear the signal. Only close friends know the path.","Moon and Rising share Aquarius, so the feeling and the face match, with no gap and no outside view: you are exactly as friendly and as detached as you seem. The Taurus Sun squares both, all three fixed, so the one light that wants comfort, touch and routine is constantly outvoted by two that want freedom and ideas. Saturn and Uranus rule the pair, which gives you discipline and invention in the same drawer.","Original loyalty. You are the friend who is unshockable, the colleague who has already thought of the next problem and the neighbour who lends the unusual tool. You keep your own counsel and your own commitments, and you do both for decades.","A doubled Aquarius can disguise a need for closeness as a preference for principles. Friends get your ideas and not your worries, and the Sun quietly resents the arrangement. Growth is telling one person, in the first person, what you are feeling today, without a theory attached."],"taurus-aquarius-pisces":["Where do I end and where does everyone else begin, and may I stand a little way off while I work it out? The Aquarius Moon asks it in the language of ideas, friendship and freedom. The Pisces Rising asks it in the language of weather, water and the faces of strangers, absorbing people so thoroughly that distance becomes a medicine. The Sun in Taurus squares the Moon and wants the answer to include dinner. You are tender and strange, and nobody is quite sure which is the disguise.","Taurus Sun and Aquarius Moon square each other, both fixed, so your will and your instincts argue stubbornly: the self wants roots and routine, the need wants air and difference. The Pisces Rising is a friendly sextile to the Sun and a neighbour to the Moon, so the manner you present is soft enough to hide the argument. Each of the three speaks a different element. The Rising makes the whole chart look more peaceful than it is.","Humane imagination. You see how people are connected and what is being missed, and you build a kind, odd, workable idea around it. You are a gentle friend who respects freedom, a good listener with unexpected opinions, and a person who is hard to categorise and easy to trust.","To protect the water, you may keep a polite distance and call it independence, or you may merge with someone and call it love. The Moon retreats, the Rising dissolves and the Sun holds firm over details. Growth is naming how much closeness you want today, and asking for it in an ordinary sentence."],"taurus-pisces-aries":["You take on the weather of every room you enter, and because the Aries Rising arrives at speed, you act on it before checking whose weather it was. A friend sighs and you are already solving it. A stranger is unhappy and you are angry on their behalf. Your Pisces Moon needs music, water, a closed door and an hour with no one, and rarely says so. The Taurus Sun keeps your feet on something solid: a meal, a garden, a routine you can touch.","The Pisces Moon sextiles the Taurus Sun, water and earth, so imagination and practicality help each other: the sensible self gives the soft one a floor. Moon and Rising are a semi-sextile, neighbouring signs that barely see each other, so your sensitivity and your directness are almost strangers. Mars rules the Rising, and fire makes your feeling louder than you intended. You cry at a song in the car, then phone the council about the broken streetlight.","Compassion that does something. You sense what is wrong, say so cleanly and then bring the soup, fix the gutter or make the call. Your imagination has a floor under it, so the lovely thing you picture tends to get made. You forgive easily, listen well and make people braver by being gentle first.","Boundaries are the lesson. You can soak up other people’s troubles, fight their battles with the Aries front and wake up exhausted by a war that was never yours. Escape may arrive as sleep, sweets or silence. Growth is asking whose feeling this is before acting, and guarding the solitude that keeps the Moon clear."],"taurus-pisces-taurus":["Picture a house with three occupants. The Sun keeps the pantry and the ledger. The Rising answers the door and says all is well. The Moon has left the back window open to the water, so the whole place smells faintly of rain. Visitors meet the front door and conclude you are unaffected. In fact you absorb a room’s mood by the second cup of tea, and you carry other people’s weather home without noticing the weight until you sit down.","Earth and water are old friends, and the Moon’s sextile to both Taurus lights means vessel and stream cooperate when you let them. Taurus supplies the body, the routine and the stubbornness to say not tonight. Pisces supplies music, imagination and the capacity to feel everything. The catch is that sextiles do nothing unless used. Skip the walk, the bath, the early night, and the feeling has nowhere to run and your calm turns to fog.","Compassion that can cook dinner. You absorb a room’s feeling and then do something concrete about it: the call, the casserole, the quiet hand on a back. You are imaginative without being flighty, kind without losing your spine, and a natural comfort to people who cannot explain what is wrong.","You may take on other people’s weather and mistake it for your own, then retreat into sleep, food or fog. The steady face shows nothing until you are overwhelmed. Growth is learning where your skin ends: leave rooms earlier, protect the quiet hour, and let others carry their feelings home."],"taurus-pisces-gemini":["Before the guest has finished saying they are fine, you are at the door with a towel, chatting about the bus so they will not have to explain their face. People see someone light and attentive. They do not see how much of the evening you carry home: the guest’s silence, a faint tremor in the host’s voice. The Pisces Moon absorbs it all, and the Taurus Sun makes it practical with soup, a blanket and a lift. Talk is how you stay afloat.","The Taurus Sun sextiles the Pisces Moon, earth steadying water, so your sensitivity has a body to live in and a kitchen to work from. The friction is between Moon and Rising. Pisces and Gemini are both mutable and square each other, Neptune’s fog against Mercury’s clarity: one dissolves, the other defines. You find the precise word for a feeling and then feel it slip away. Rest comes when the Sun makes you sit.","Practical compassion. You sense what a room needs and have it ready, and you find the words that make a hard thing speakable without making it smaller. You are a gifted comforter, a translator between moods, and the friend whose house is warm at midnight.","You take on a mood and mistake it for your own, then talk faster to stay above it. The Taurus Sun can dig in against changes you have not yet admitted you want, while the Gemini surface promises more than the Pisces Moon can carry. Growth is solitude on purpose: an hour with water, music or an empty room, and nobody to translate for."],"taurus-pisces-cancer":["People assume you are easy-going because you rarely argue and nearly always listen. They are half right. The Cancer Rising offers a soft welcome, and the Pisces Moon takes in every mood in the room, including the ones nobody voiced, so often there is nothing left to argue about. What they miss is the Taurus Sun, a warm stone in the current. The water flows around it and it does not move. Your yes is feeling, not consent.","Water dominates here. The Pisces Moon and the Cancer Rising are a trine, the same element, and their agreement is nearly seamless, which is why boundaries seem to dissolve before you notice. The Taurus Sun cooperates with both from the earth side, and it is the reason the flooding never fully carries you off. Because the Moon rules your Rising, whatever the Moon takes in shows on your face within minutes.","Compassion with a floor. You feel what others feel and still cook dinner, which is rarer than it sounds. You are the friend people tell the thing they cannot tell anyone else, and you hold it with the care of someone who will still be there on Tuesday. Music, water and beauty restore you, and you pass the restoration on.","You may absorb what is not yours, then refuse, in a sudden Taurus way, to explain why you are tired. Moods from the room settle in your body as if they were your own, and the Cancer front keeps serving the whole time. Growth is stepping out of the room before the fatigue arrives, and learning which feelings were yours."],"taurus-pisces-leo":["At three in the morning the evening finally stops, and you notice how much of it came home with you: the cracked laugh at the corner table, the friend who said fine too quickly. The Leo Rising spent the night being warm and bright. The Pisces Moon took in everyone’s weather. The Taurus Sun is what gets up and makes breakfast, steady in a way the other two can lean on.","Taurus and Pisces sextile, so Sun and Moon cooperate gently: the Sun gives the Moon’s softness a body, a routine and a garden, and the Moon gives the Sun a reason to be kind. Leo Rising squares the Sun and sits a quincunx from the Moon, so it understands neither. It wants brightness and applause where the Moon wants water and quiet. You manage by being sociable on a schedule and retreating to the real thing afterwards.","Warmth that actually listens. You walk into a room as a light and move through it as a sponge, so people feel both lifted and understood. You make beauty and kindness out of ordinary materials, and you put your senses to work on other people’s comfort.","The Moon absorbs what belongs to others while the Rising performs being fine, so the tiredness has no visible cause. The Sun resists changing the arrangement even when it is the arrangement that leaks. Growth is leaving an event at the point of fullness, and calling the quiet an appointment rather than a retreat."],"taurus-pisces-virgo":["You tidy because the world is too much, and you call it being practical. The Virgo Rising scrubs, sorts and fixes, and the Pisces Moon, directly opposite, feels everything the room is carrying and dissolves into it. Both are true. The Taurus Sun is the oak table in the middle, scrubbed and solid, where the two finally sit down. People see a competent person. You know how much of the competence is a wall against the water.","Virgo Rising and Pisces Moon stand opposite each other, both mutable: order against dissolution, analysis against absorption. The Taurus Sun trines the Rising and sextiles the Moon, so it cooperates with both and gives you a place to stand. That is the gift of this chart: the practical half and the dreamy half are on speaking terms because the Sun speaks both languages. Mercury rules the Rising, so you translate feeling into a to-do list, and sometimes it works.","Practical compassion. You feel what someone needs and then actually do it: the meal, the form, the lift to the station. People find you easy to be sad around, because you neither fix them nor flinch. You are also good with music, water and quiet, in measured doses.","The Moon takes in everyone’s weather and the Rising answers by rearranging the furniture, so the real feeling goes unspoken under a busy afternoon. The Sun adds a dislike of being hurried into change. Growth is sitting still with the unsorted feeling for ten minutes before you do anything about it."],"taurus-pisces-libra":["Three voices share the house and no two of them speak the same language. The Libra Rising talks in compliments, compromises and good taste. The Pisces Moon speaks in feelings that belong to everyone in the room and in music nobody else can hear. The Taurus Sun speaks in plain preferences about dinner, and is, to everyone’s relief, usually right. You are lovely company and difficult to pin down.","This chart is a yod by sign: the Taurus Sun and the Pisces Moon sextile each other, an easy and gentle angle, and both stand five signs from the Libra Rising at the point of the shape. The Rising is the one that must keep adjusting, making a fair, pleasant face out of a sensual practicality and a very porous sensitivity. Venus rules Sun and Rising, so beauty carries the translation, and the angle keeps asking for one more compromise.","Gentle diplomacy. You feel the room, soften what needs softening and keep a calm centre while others are upset. You make beauty out of ordinary things, listen to what is not said, and are generous without keeping score.","The front is always balanced and the inside is not, so people may not know when you are overwhelmed. The Moon absorbs what is around it, the Rising keeps the room pleasant, and the Sun quietly skips its own comforts. Growth is leaving the room before you are depleted, and calling that an appointment with yourself."],"taurus-pisces-scorpio":["You stop with your hand raised at a friend’s door, because you can already feel the mood in the kitchen, and you arrive carrying it. The Pisces Moon absorbs the weather of every room. The Scorpio Rising decides how much of it shows, which is almost none, so you look composed while taking in everyone’s trouble. The Sun in Taurus is the stabiliser, wanting bread, music, a long bath and one day with nobody’s emotions in it.","Water holds two of the three lights: Pisces Moon and Scorpio Rising are a trine, so the feeling and the face flow together, and the two of them can run a whole inner life without consulting the Sun. The Taurus Sun faces the Rising across the wheel and sits one sign from the Moon, an earthy anchor that gives the water a shore. It is a dependable arrangement with one leak: you take on other people’s pain without noticing and call the heaviness your own.","Compassion with a spine. You feel what others feel, and you can still hold the line. That makes you a gifted listener and a friend in hard seasons, someone who can sit with grief without drowning in it and who makes plain things, like bread and music, feel like small ceremonies.","The boundary between your feelings and everyone else’s blurs, and the Rising hides the evidence, so exhaustion arrives with no visible cause. You may escape into sleep, music or comfort food rather than say the sentence that would protect you. Growth is a daily habit of asking whose mood this is, and leaving the room to find out."],"taurus-pisces-sagittarius":["People hear the cheerful certainty of the Sagittarius Rising and assume you know exactly where you are going. Mostly you are following a feeling, and the Pisces Moon is both the compass and the weather. It absorbs the moods in the room and turns them into music, kindness or an inexplicable need to leave early. The Sun in Taurus is the loom that holds the thread: it keeps the bills paid, the meals made and the routines gentle enough to rest in. You look like a leap. You are a very careful catcher.","Jupiter rules your Rising and, in the older scheme, your Moon too, so faith and feeling speak the same dialect, yet the two make a square, both mutable, so the face you show and the water you feel keep crossing paths in the corridor. The Taurus Sun is a sextile to the Moon, a supportive angle that gives the water something to run on. Three different elements and no shared ground between Sun and Rising ask for constant translation. When the Sun builds a small routine around the Moon’s sensitivity, the Rising has room to shine.","Compassion with a plan for dinner. You are a natural encourager, artist, storyteller and carer, and you make hope feel physical: a warm meal, a song, a hand on the shoulder. You can enter someone else’s sorrow without drowning, and then put the kettle on.","Absorbing everyone’s weather while telling everyone it is sunny can leave you exhausted by something nobody can see. The Sun’s habits then become a way of avoiding the subject. Growth is a daily moment of checking which of the moods in you actually belong to you, and telling at least one person the truth about the answer."],"taurus-pisces-capricorn":["At four on a winter afternoon, as the light goes and the rain starts, you put on the lamp, and the room fills with everyone’s unspoken mood. The Pisces Moon absorbs it all and turns it into a song hummed in the kitchen. The Capricorn Rising makes sure the lamp is paid for and the roof checked. The Sun in Taurus bridges the two, sextile to the Moon and trine to the Rising. The world meets a capable grown-up. Those who stay a while meet the one who hums.","This is an arc of ease: the Taurus Sun is sextile to the Pisces Moon and trine to the Capricorn Rising, and Moon and Rising are also sextile, so the three lights cooperate in an unusually friendly way. The Sun is the bridge between feeling and form, building things the water can rest in. Each light supports the others, which is generous, but also means the difficult conversation can go unwitnessed. Saturn gives the water banks, and the water gives Saturn a reason.","Compassion with infrastructure. You feel what people need and arrange for them to get it: the appointment, the meal, the quiet room. You are artistic and dependable in the same week, gentle in a crisis, and a natural builder of places where fragile things can be safe.","Too much ease can mean too little challenge. You absorb other people’s feelings through the Moon, hide the evidence through the Rising, and the Sun keeps everything running. Exhaustion arrives with a smile. Growth is protecting a quiet evening as seriously as a deadline, and leaving the room when the mood is not yours."],"taurus-pisces-aquarius":["When you are overwhelmed you become extra friendly, and then you quietly vanish. The Pisces Moon soaks up other people’s moods until you cannot tell which are yours, and needs solitude, water and music to settle. The Aquarius Rising makes sure that none of this shows: you seem sunny, original and slightly elsewhere. Your Taurus Sun is the bell in the valley, warm and unhurried, ringing the same note whatever the weather, so that the Moon always has somewhere to come home to.","Taurus Sun and Pisces Moon are a sextile, so who you are becoming and what soothes you cooperate gently: sensory comfort, music, a body at rest. The Aquarius Rising stands one sign from the Moon and squares the Sun, so the cool, friendly manner is a poor match for a feeling this porous, and a worse match for a Sun that wants things to stay. The Rising keeps the manner so friendly that nobody thinks to ask how you are.","Gentle originality. You offer compassion without sentimentality and ideas without arrogance. You are good with animals, children, strangers and creative people, and your calm, unhurried presence makes unusual things feel safe and ordinary things feel like gifts.","Absorbing everyone’s weather behind a cheerful, detached face makes you tired in ways that are hard to explain. You may withdraw instead of asking, and call the withdrawal independence. Growth is naming the overwhelm to one person before you vanish, and letting them be the door that opens from the street."],"taurus-pisces-pisces":["Three voices share a small boat. The Taurus Sun sits in the middle with the oars and a flask of tea, insisting on a regular route. The Pisces Moon trails a hand in the water, feeling whatever the river feels. The Pisces Rising sits at the prow, waving at every passing boat and taking on the mood of each. The result is a very gentle crew with a very stubborn pilot. Strangers feel welcomed. Those who sail with you learn that the route is not negotiable.","Moon and Rising share Pisces, so the feeling and the face match, with no gap and no outside view: you are exactly as receptive as you appear. The Sun is a sextile to both, a supportive angle that gives the water a shore, a routine and a body. Jupiter and Neptune rule the pair, which makes empathy easy and boundaries a skill to be learned in adult life, the way some people learn to swim.","Unforced tenderness. You make people feel safe, listened to and unhurried, and you can turn a plain room into a place where it is all right to cry. Your Sun lends it structure, so you keep your word and your appointments. Artists, carers and anyone far from home do well beside you.","Two lights of water mean that other people’s feelings arrive as your own, and the Sun’s loyalty makes it hard to leave a weather system you have already moved into. You may stay too long in the wrong climate. Growth is learning where the shore is, and standing on it daily for ten minutes with no mood in your pocket."]});
